msgstr "A heavy shaft made from scrap metal.  It needs arrowheads and fletching to become a functional arrow."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "unfletched fire-hardened wooden arrow"
msgid_plural "unfletched fire-hardened wooden arrows"
msgstr[0] "unfletched fire-hardened wooden arrow"
msgstr[1] "unfletched fire-hardened wooden arrows"

#. ~ Description for unfletched fire-hardened wooden arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A simple arrow shaft that has had a point carved into it and then fire-"
"hardened.  It needs fletching to be worth firing from a bow."
msgstr "A simple arrow shaft that has had a point carved into it and then fire-hardened.  It needs fletching to be worth firing from a bow."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "unfletched field point wooden arrow"
msgid_plural "unfletched field point wooden arrows"
msgstr[0] "unfletched field point wooden arrow"
msgstr[1] "unfletched field point wooden arrows"

#. ~ Description for unfletched field point wooden arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A simple arrow shaft that has a crude arrowhead.  Useful for hunting small "
"woodland creatures, but needs fletching before it is worth firing."
msgstr "A simple arrow shaft that has a crude arrowhead.  Useful for hunting small woodland creatures, but needs fletching before it is worth firing."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "unfletched small game arrow"
msgid_plural "unfletched small game arrows"
msgstr[0] "unfletched small game arrow"
msgstr[1] "unfletched small game arrows"

#. ~ Description for unfletched small game arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A simple arrow shaft that has a wide blunt head.  Useful for hunting small "
"woodland creatures without splattering them all over the ground, but needs "
"fletching before it is worth firing."
msgstr "A simple arrow shaft that has a wide blunt head.  Useful for hunting small woodland creatures without splattering them all over the ground, but needs fletching before it is worth firing."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "fire-hardened wooden arrow"
msgid_plural "fire-hardened wooden arrows"
msgstr[0] "fire-hardened wooden arrow"
msgstr[1] "fire-hardened wooden arrows"

#. ~ Description for fire-hardened wooden arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This simple arrow has a fire-hardened point and fletching.  Stands a below "
"average chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "This simple arrow has a fire-hardened point and fletching.  Stands a below average chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "field point wooden arrow"
msgid_plural "field point wooden arrows"
msgstr[0] "field point wooden arrow"
msgstr[1] "field point wooden arrows"

#. ~ Description for field point wooden arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A simple arrow shaft that has a crude arrowhead and fletching.  Useful for "
"hunting small woodland creatures or as a last ditch defense against zombies."
"  Stands a below average chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "A simple arrow shaft that has a crude arrowhead and fletching.  Useful for hunting small woodland creatures or as a last ditch defense against zombies.  Stands a below average chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "small game arrow"
msgid_plural "small game arrows"
msgstr[0] "small game arrow"
msgstr[1] "small game arrows"

#. ~ Description for small game arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A simple arrow shaft that has a wide blunt head.  Useful for hunting small "
"woodland creatures without splattering them all over the ground, but stands "
"a below average chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "A simple arrow shaft that has a wide blunt head.  Useful for hunting small woodland creatures without splattering them all over the ground, but stands a below average chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "wooden arrow"
msgid_plural "wooden arrows"
msgstr[0] "wooden arrow"
msgstr[1] "wooden arrows"

#. ~ Description for wooden arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A basic wooden arrow, it has a metal arrowhead and fletching.  It's light-"
"weight, does some damage, and is so-so on accuracy.  Stands a below average "
"chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "A basic wooden arrow, it has a metal arrowhead and fletching.  It's light-weight, does some damage, and is so-so on accuracy.  Stands a below average chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "heavy fire-hardened arrow"
msgid_plural "heavy fire-hardened arrows"
msgstr[0] "heavy fire-hardened arrow"
msgstr[1] "heavy fire-hardened arrows"

#. ~ Description for heavy fire-hardened arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This arrow is significantly sturdier than other wooden arrows.  It has a "
"fire-hardened point and fletching.  Stands a good chance of remaining intact"
" once fired."
msgstr "This arrow is significantly sturdier than other wooden arrows.  It has a fire-hardened point and fletching.  Stands a good chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "unfletched heavy fire-hardened arrow"
msgid_plural "unfletched heavy fire-hardened arrows"
msgstr[0] "unfletched heavy fire-hardened arrow"
msgstr[1] "unfletched heavy fire-hardened arrows"

#. ~ Description for unfletched heavy fire-hardened arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This arrow is significantly sturdier than other wooden arrows.  It has a "
"fire-hardened point, but needs fletching to be worth firing."
msgstr "This arrow is significantly sturdier than other wooden arrows.  It has a fire-hardened point, but needs fletching to be worth firing."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "unfletched heavy field point arrow"
msgid_plural "unfletched heavy field point arrows"
msgstr[0] "unfletched heavy field point arrow"
msgstr[1] "unfletched heavy field point arrows"

#. ~ Description for unfletched heavy field point arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This arrow is significantly sturdier than other wooden arrows.  It has a "
"field point tip, but needs fletching before it is worth firing."
msgstr "This arrow is significantly sturdier than other wooden arrows.  It has a field point tip, but needs fletching before it is worth firing."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "heavy field point arrow"
msgid_plural "heavy field point arrows"
msgstr[0] "heavy field point arrow"
msgstr[1] "heavy field point arrows"

#. ~ Description for heavy field point arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This arrow is significantly sturdier than other wooden arrows.  It has a "
"crude field point head and fletching.  Stands a good chance of remaining "
"intact once fired."
msgstr "This arrow is significantly sturdier than other wooden arrows.  It has a crude field point head and fletching.  Stands a good chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "heavy wooden arrow"
msgid_plural "heavy wooden arrows"
msgstr[0] "heavy wooden arrow"
msgstr[1] "heavy wooden arrows"

#. ~ Description for heavy wooden arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A heavy wooden arrow, with fletching and a metal arrowhead.  It's much "
"heavier than other wooden arrows, and as a result it does more damage and is"
" more stable in flight, resulting in better accuracy over a longer range.  "
"Stands a good chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "A heavy wooden arrow, with fletching and a metal arrowhead.  It's much heavier than other wooden arrows, and as a result it does more damage and is more stable in flight, resulting in better accuracy over a longer range.  Stands a good chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "unfletched sharpened metal arrow"
msgid_plural "unfletched sharpened metal arrows"
msgstr[0] "unfletched sharpened metal arrow"
msgstr[1] "unfletched sharpened metal arrows"

#. ~ Description for unfletched sharpened metal arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This metal shaft has been carefully sharpened so that it has a crude point "
"at the end.  It needs fletching to be worth firing from a bow."
msgstr "This metal shaft has been carefully sharpened so that it has a crude point at the end.  It needs fletching to be worth firing from a bow."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "sharpened metal arrow"
msgid_plural "sharpened metal arrows"
msgstr[0] "sharpened metal arrow"
msgstr[1] "sharpened metal arrows"

#. ~ Description for sharpened metal arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This metal shaft has been carefully sharpened so that it has a crude point "
"at the end.  Stands a very good chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "This metal shaft has been carefully sharpened so that it has a crude point at the end.  Stands a very good chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "metal arrow"
msgid_plural "metal arrows"
msgstr[0] "metal arrow"
msgstr[1] "metal arrows"

#. ~ Description for metal arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This metal arrow has fletching and a steel arrowhead.  Stands a very good "
"chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "This metal arrow has fletching and a steel arrowhead.  Stands a very good chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "carbon fiber arrow"
msgid_plural "carbon fiber arrows"
msgstr[0] "carbon fiber arrow"
msgstr[1] "carbon fiber arrows"

#. ~ Description for carbon fiber arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"High-tech carbon fiber shafts and 100 grain broadheads.  Very lightweight, "
"fast, and notoriously fragile.  Stands a bad chance of remaining intact once"
" fired."
msgstr "High-tech carbon fiber shafts and 100 grain broadheads.  Very lightweight, fast, and notoriously fragile.  Stands a bad chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "exploding arrow"
msgid_plural "exploding arrows"
msgstr[0] "exploding arrow"
msgstr[1] "exploding arrows"

#. ~ Description for exploding arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This arrow has a small IED strapped to its tip.  Horribly inaccurate, heavy,"
" and bulky, not only does this contraption require expert hands to pull off "
"a shot, it requires one to loose this with a small measure of confidence the"
" shooter won't be caught in the blast radius."
msgstr "This arrow has a small IED strapped to its tip.  Horribly inaccurate, heavy, and bulky, not only does this contraption require expert hands to pull off a shot, it requires one to loose this with a small measure of confidence the shooter won't be caught in the blast radius."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "flaming arrow"
msgid_plural "flaming arrows"
msgstr[0] "flaming arrow"
msgstr[1] "flaming arrows"

#. ~ Description for flaming arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This arrow has a flaming rag wrapped around the shaft near the head.  You "
"should shoot it soon before it burns your bow."
msgstr "This arrow has a flaming rag wrapped around the shaft near the head.  You should shoot it soon before it burns your bow."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "wooden crossbow bolt"
msgid_plural "wooden crossbow bolts"
msgstr[0] "wooden crossbow bolt"
msgstr[1] "wooden crossbow bolts"

#. ~ Description for wooden crossbow bolt
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sharpened bolt carved from wood.  It's very light, but doesn't do much "
"damage and isn't particularly accurate.  Stands a below average chance of "
"remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "A sharpened bolt carved from wood.  It's very light, but doesn't do much damage and isn't particularly accurate.  Stands a below average chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "metal crossbow bolt"
msgid_plural "metal crossbow bolts"
msgstr[0] "metal crossbow bolt"
msgstr[1] "metal crossbow bolts"

#. ~ Description for metal crossbow bolt
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sharpened bolt made from metal of some kind.  It's heavy and unwieldy, "
"providing moderate damage and accuracy.  Stands a very good chance of "
"remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "A sharpened bolt made from metal of some kind.  It's heavy and unwieldy, providing moderate damage and accuracy.  Stands a very good chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "steel crossbow bolt"
msgid_plural "steel crossbow bolts"
msgstr[0] "steel crossbow bolt"
msgstr[1] "steel crossbow bolts"

#. ~ Description for steel crossbow bolt
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sharp bolt made from steel.  Deadly in skilled hands.  Stands an excellent"
" chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "A sharp bolt made from steel.  Deadly in skilled hands.  Stands an excellent chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "explosive crossbow bolt"
msgid_plural "explosive crossbow bolts"
msgstr[0] "explosive crossbow bolt"
msgstr[1] "explosive crossbow bolts"

#. ~ Description for explosive crossbow bolt
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A lightweight, sharpened bolt made from some kind of metal.  It is fairly "
"unwieldy and only provides moderate accuracy, due to being filled with "
"explosives and fitted with an impact trigger."
msgstr "A lightweight, sharpened bolt made from some kind of metal.  It is fairly unwieldy and only provides moderate accuracy, due to being filled with explosives and fitted with an impact trigger."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "plastic shaft"
msgid_plural "plastic shafts"
msgstr[0] "plastic shaft"
msgstr[1] "plastic shafts"

#. ~ Description for plastic shaft
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A crude shaft made from plastic.  It needs arrowheads and fletching to "
"become a functional arrow."
msgstr "A crude shaft made from plastic.  It needs arrowheads and fletching to become a functional arrow."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "plastic arrowhead"
msgid_plural "plastic arrowheads"
msgstr[0] "plastic arrowhead"
msgstr[1] "plastic arrowheads"

#. ~ Description for plastic arrowhead
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Plastic heads for an arrow.  Placing these on arrows will make them more "
"damaging and piercing."
msgstr "Plastic heads for an arrow.  Placing these on arrows will make them more damaging and piercing."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "throwing knife"
msgid_plural "throwing knives"
msgstr[0] "throwing knife"
msgstr[1] "throwing knives"

#. ~ Description for throwing knife
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A thin and flat knife made for throwing.  Its ineffective cutting edge and "
"odd shape makes it unsuitable for use as a tool."
msgstr "A thin and flat knife made for throwing.  Its ineffective cutting edge and odd shape makes it unsuitable for use as a tool."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "throwing axe"
msgid_plural "throwing axes"
msgstr[0] "throwing axe"
msgstr[1] "throwing axes"

#. ~ Description for throwing axe
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A lightweight hatchet made for throwing.  Its ineffective cutting edge and "
"light weight makes it unsuitable for use as a tool."
msgstr "A lightweight hatchet made for throwing.  Its ineffective cutting edge and light weight makes it unsuitable for use as a tool."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "lawn dart"
msgid_plural "lawn darts"
msgstr[0] "lawn dart"
msgstr[1] "lawn darts"

#. ~ Description for lawn dart
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "A large plastic dart made for outdoor games."
msgstr "A large plastic dart made for outdoor games."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "wooden fishing spear"
msgid_plural "wooden fishing spears"
msgstr[0] "wooden fishing spear"
msgstr[1] "wooden fishing spears"

#. ~ Description for wooden fishing spear
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An underwater fishing spear made from wood tipped with steel.  It's very "
"light, but doesn't have much range.  Stands a below average chance of "
"remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "An underwater fishing spear made from wood tipped with steel.  It's very light, but doesn't have much range.  Stands a below average chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "metal fishing spear"
msgid_plural "metal fishing spears"
msgstr[0] "metal fishing spear"
msgstr[1] "metal fishing spears"

#. ~ Description for metal fishing spear
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An underwater fishing spear made from metal.  It's light, but doesn't have "
"much range.  Stands a very good chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "An underwater fishing spear made from metal.  It's light, but doesn't have much range.  Stands a very good chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "carbon fiber fishing spear"
msgid_plural "carbon fiber fishing spears"
msgstr[0] "carbon fiber fishing spear"
msgstr[1] "carbon fiber fishing spears"

#. ~ Description for carbon fiber fishing spear
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An underwater fishing spear made from carbon fiber.  It's very light, but "
"doesn't have much range.  Stands a bad chance of remaining intact once "
"fired."
msgstr "An underwater fishing spear made from carbon fiber.  It's very light, but doesn't have much range.  Stands a bad chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "plastic arrow"
msgid_plural "plastic arrows"
msgstr[0] "plastic arrow"
msgstr[1] "plastic arrows"

#. ~ Description for plastic arrow
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This plastic arrow has a plastic arrowhead and fletching.  Stands a good "
"chance of remaining intact once fired."
msgstr "This plastic arrow has a plastic arrowhead and fletching.  Stands a good chance of remaining intact once fired."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "sulfur"
msgid_plural "sulfur"
msgstr[0] "sulfur"
msgstr[1] "sulfur"

#. ~ Description for sulfur
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of yellow grains of pure sulfur.  Primarily used to make battery "
"acid, sulfur is sometimes used as fuel for explosives.  Can be burned to "
"produce acidic smoke, that is deadly to bacteria and humans alike, or "
"oxidized to make paper-bleaching agents."
msgstr "A handful of yellow grains of pure sulfur.  Primarily used to make battery acid, sulfur is sometimes used as fuel for explosives.  Can be burned to produce acidic smoke, that is deadly to bacteria and humans alike, or oxidized to make paper-bleaching agents."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "cement"
msgid_plural "cement"
msgstr[0] "cement"
msgstr[1] "cement"

#. ~ Description for cement
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Portland is most likely long gone, but its memory persists in cement.  This "
"ubiquitous binder can be used for all kinds of advanced masonry.  Just add "
"water."
msgstr "Portland is most likely long gone, but its memory persists in cement.  This ubiquitous binder can be used for all kinds of advanced masonry.  Just add water."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "limestone"
msgid_plural "limestone"
msgstr[0] "limestone"
msgstr[1] "limestone"

#. ~ Description for limestone
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of small chunks of limestone.  Useful for experiments at science "
"fairs, but pretty useless as ammo.  Maybe something could be crafted from "
"this stuff…"
msgstr "A handful of small chunks of limestone.  Useful for experiments at science fairs, but pretty useless as ammo.  Maybe something could be crafted from this stuff…"

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "quicklime"
msgid_plural "quicklime"
msgstr[0] "quicklime"
msgstr[1] "quicklime"

#. ~ Description for quicklime
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The product of burning limestone, this white powder is a crucial ingredient "
"in making cement.  That said, it is also extremely caustic and will cause "
"severe burns to any tissue it comes in contact with.  This property could "
"probably be exploited..."
msgstr "The product of burning limestone, this white powder is a crucial ingredient in making cement.  That said, it is also extremely caustic and will cause severe burns to any tissue it comes in contact with.  This property could probably be exploited..."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py lang/json/terrain_from_json.py
msgid "sand"
msgid_plural "sand"
msgstr[0] "sand"
msgstr[1] "sand"

#. ~ Description for sand
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of New England sand.  If you had a stoked furnace, you could turn "
"it into glass.  Otherwise, it's only good for making cement."
msgstr "A handful of New England sand.  If you had a stoked furnace, you could turn it into glass.  Otherwise, it's only good for making cement."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "aluminum powder"
msgid_plural "aluminum powder"
msgstr[0] "aluminum powder"
msgstr[1] "aluminum powder"

#. ~ Description for aluminum powder
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of finely ground aluminum powder.  This strong reducing agent was "
"used in combination with various oxidants for chemical welding and "
"explosives alike.  Just before the Cataclysm, however, it was the basis of "
"virtually all commercial metallic-hued paints and anti-corrosive coatings."
msgstr "A handful of finely ground aluminum powder.  This strong reducing agent was used in combination with various oxidants for chemical welding and explosives alike.  Just before the Cataclysm, however, it was the basis of virtually all commercial metallic-hued paints and anti-corrosive coatings."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "zinc powder"
msgid_plural "zinc powder"
msgstr[0] "zinc powder"
msgstr[1] "zinc powder"

#. ~ Description for zinc powder
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of zinc powder.  While commercially used mostly in cosmetics and "
"for paints, hobbyists used to mix it with sulfur to make basic rocket fuel /"
" smokescreen.  When treated with a strong acid, it will produce hydrogen."
msgstr "A handful of zinc powder.  While commercially used mostly in cosmetics and for paints, hobbyists used to mix it with sulfur to make basic rocket fuel / smokescreen.  When treated with a strong acid, it will produce hydrogen."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "sulfuric acid"
msgid_plural "sulfuric acid"
msgstr[0] "sulfuric acid"
msgstr[1] "sulfuric acid"

#. ~ Description for sulfuric acid
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Sulfuric acid: viscous, foul-smelling and extremely corrosive, particularly "
"to organic matter and evil clowns.  Although used to prepare a number of "
"chemicals, it is mostly known as battery acid, due to its widest commercial "
"application."
msgstr "Sulfuric acid: viscous, foul-smelling and extremely corrosive, particularly to organic matter and evil clowns.  Although used to prepare a number of chemicals, it is mostly known as battery acid, due to its widest commercial application."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "acetone"
msgid_plural "acetone"
msgstr[0] "acetone"
msgstr[1] "acetone"

#. ~ Description for acetone
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Acetone, best known as the primary constituent of most nail polish removers."
"  Flammable and can be easily used for potent home-made explosives, as "
"demonstrated by the terrorist attacks of 2016."
msgstr "Acetone, best known as the primary constituent of most nail polish removers.  Flammable and can be easily used for potent home-made explosives, as demonstrated by the terrorist attacks of 2016."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "nitric acid"
msgid_plural "nitric acid"
msgstr[0] "nitric acid"
msgstr[1] "nitric acid"

#. ~ Description for nitric acid
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Nitric acid, a strong oxidant and extremely corrosive material.  Mainly used"
" in the production of synthetic fertilizers, for etching of circuit boards "
"and in woodworking.  Remains quite useful both for making a vast array of "
"pyrotechnic and explosive agents and as a direct weapon: not many beings "
"enjoy being doused in nitric acid."
msgstr "Nitric acid, a strong oxidant and extremely corrosive material.  Mainly used in the production of synthetic fertilizers, for etching of circuit boards and in woodworking.  Remains quite useful both for making a vast array of pyrotechnic and explosive agents and as a direct weapon: not many beings enjoy being doused in nitric acid."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "chromium oxide"
msgid_plural "chromium oxide"
msgstr[0] "chromium oxide"
msgstr[1] "chromium oxide"

#. ~ Description for chromium oxide
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of chromium oxide pellets.  This substance, typically known as the"
" only stable green pigment for paints, is also a mild oxidizer, which can be"
" mixed with aluminum powder to make thermite for welding.  If one had access"
" to a CVD machine and a laboratory worth of reagents, they might be able to "
"produce very durable ceramic layers."
msgstr "A handful of chromium oxide pellets.  This substance, typically known as the only stable green pigment for paints, is also a mild oxidizer, which can be mixed with aluminum powder to make thermite for welding.  If one had access to a CVD machine and a laboratory worth of reagents, they might be able to produce very durable ceramic layers."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "calcium carbide"
msgid_plural "calcium carbide"
msgstr[0] "calcium carbide"
msgstr[1] "calcium carbide"

#. ~ Description for calcium carbide
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of calcium carbide chunks, giving off a faint, garlic-like smell."
"  Commercially, calcium carbide was used for on-the-spot manufacture of "
"acetylene and historically to power acetylene lamps.  If mixed with water "
"and sealed, it will explode with little strength, but with relatively loud "
"noise and could maybe be used as a decoy..."
msgstr "A handful of calcium carbide chunks, giving off a faint, garlic-like smell.  Commercially, calcium carbide was used for on-the-spot manufacture of acetylene and historically to power acetylene lamps.  If mixed with water and sealed, it will explode with little strength, but with relatively loud noise and could maybe be used as a decoy..."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py lang/json/ammunition_type_from_json.py
msgid "hexamine"
msgid_plural "hexamine"
msgstr[0] "hexamine"
msgstr[1] "hexamine"

#. ~ Description for hexamine
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of waxy hexamine tablets.  This ubiquitous fuel was used to start "
"up almost every garden grill and no 'real' camping trip could do its cooking"
" without it, until the Cataclysm.  Nowadays, it is even more valuable then "
"before, being the key component in the preparation of several military-grade"
" explosives."
msgstr "A handful of waxy hexamine tablets.  This ubiquitous fuel was used to start up almost every garden grill and no 'real' camping trip could do its cooking without it, until the Cataclysm.  Nowadays, it is even more valuable then before, being the key component in the preparation of several military-grade explosives."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgid_plural "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgstr[0] "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgstr[1] "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"

#. ~ Description for hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Concentrated hydrogen peroxide is a powerful oxidant, violently decomposing "
"in contact with most reducing agents.  Can be used as rocket fuel or to make"
" high explosives.  Causes severe burns to any organic matter and may ignite "
"it on contact."
msgstr "Concentrated hydrogen peroxide is a powerful oxidant, violently decomposing in contact with most reducing agents.  Can be used as rocket fuel or to make high explosives.  Causes severe burns to any organic matter and may ignite it on contact."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "ammonium nitrate"
msgid_plural "ammonium nitrate"
msgstr[0] "ammonium nitrate"
msgstr[1] "ammonium nitrate"

#. ~ Description for ammonium nitrate
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of ammonium nitrate.  This white, crystalline powder is commonly "
"used as a component of fertilizers and explosives.  Could also be dissolved "
"in water to sharply lower its temperature, but is there any use for this "
"quality in this new world?"
msgstr "A handful of ammonium nitrate.  This white, crystalline powder is commonly used as a component of fertilizers and explosives.  Could also be dissolved in water to sharply lower its temperature, but is there any use for this quality in this new world?"

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "saltpeter"
msgid_plural "saltpeter"
msgstr[0] "saltpeter"
msgstr[1] "saltpeter"

#. ~ Description for saltpeter
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of saltpeter.  Sometimes used as a fertilizer, this ubiquitous "
"nitrate is the principal constituent of black gunpowder and simple rocket "
"propellants, such as rocket candy."
msgstr "A handful of saltpeter.  Sometimes used as a fertilizer, this ubiquitous nitrate is the principal constituent of black gunpowder and simple rocket propellants, such as rocket candy."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "aluminum sulfate"
msgid_plural "aluminum sulfate"
msgstr[0] "aluminum sulfate"
msgstr[1] "aluminum sulfate"

#. ~ Description for aluminum sulfate
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Several crystals of aluminum sulfate.  Historically, an agent for purifying "
"water and as molluscicide, due to the fact that it degenerates their slime."
"  Just before the Cataclysm, its main uses were for adjusting the acidity of"
" the soil and as an additive to baking powder.  If mixed with a strong acid,"
" it could be used to saturate the soil with aluminum, causing all but the "
"most resistant of plants to wither and die."
msgstr "Several crystals of aluminum sulfate.  Historically, an agent for purifying water and as molluscicide, due to the fact that it degenerates their slime.  Just before the Cataclysm, its main uses were for adjusting the acidity of the soil and as an additive to baking powder.  If mixed with a strong acid, it could be used to saturate the soil with aluminum, causing all but the most resistant of plants to wither and die."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "acetic acid"
msgid_plural "acetic acid"
msgstr[0] "acetic acid"
msgstr[1] "acetic acid"

#. ~ Description for acetic acid
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Concentrated acetic acid, typically used as a chemical reagent and "
"antifungal agent.  Despite its horrid smell, it was used to prepare several "
"types of perfumes, but would making perfume not be too ...fancy for "
"postapocalyptic New England?"
msgstr "Concentrated acetic acid, typically used as a chemical reagent and antifungal agent.  Despite its horrid smell, it was used to prepare several types of perfumes, but would making perfume not be too ...fancy for postapocalyptic New England?"

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "thermite"
msgid_plural "thermite"
msgstr[0] "thermite"
msgstr[1] "thermite"

#. ~ Description for thermite
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of silvery-greenish powder, produced by mixing aluminum and "
"chromium oxide.  This mixture, burning at a constant pace and at extremely "
"high temperature, was once used for on-the-spot welding.  Can be used as an "
"incendiary material in a pinch."
msgstr "A handful of silvery-greenish powder, produced by mixing aluminum and chromium oxide.  This mixture, burning at a constant pace and at extremely high temperature, was once used for on-the-spot welding.  Can be used as an incendiary material in a pinch."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "ANFO"
msgid_plural "ANFO"
msgstr[0] "ANFO"
msgstr[1] "ANFO"

#. ~ Description for ANFO
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Several brownish pellets that were made by absorbing organic fuel on "
"ammonium nitrate.  This ammonium nitrate–fuel oil or ANFO, as it is called, "
"mixture is a common industrial explosive due to its stability and low price."
"  Burns fast, but needs an explosive primer to detonate..."
msgstr "Several brownish pellets that were made by absorbing organic fuel on ammonium nitrate.  This ammonium nitrate–fuel oil or ANFO, as it is called, mixture is a common industrial explosive due to its stability and low price.  Burns fast, but needs an explosive primer to detonate..."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "black gunpowder"
msgid_plural "black gunpowder"
msgstr[0] "black gunpowder"
msgstr[1] "black gunpowder"

#. ~ Description for black gunpowder
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A handful of black gunpowder, made by mixing charcoal and sulfur with "
"saltpeter.  Pretty useless for making modern cartridges, as the soot "
"produced when it burns will quickly clog any firearm, but it could be used "
"to make some vicious bombs."
msgstr "A handful of black gunpowder, made by mixing charcoal and sulfur with saltpeter.  Pretty useless for making modern cartridges, as the soot produced when it burns will quickly clog any firearm, but it could be used to make some vicious bombs."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "RDX"
msgid_plural "RDX"
msgstr[0] "RDX"
msgstr[1] "RDX"

#. ~ Description for RDX
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Several off-white crystals of RDX or hexogen--a military-grade, shelf-stable"
" high explosive.  Can be cast into shaped charges or mixed with scrap to "
"pepper the blast area with high-velocity shrapnel."
msgstr "Several off-white crystals of RDX or hexogen--a military-grade, shelf-stable high explosive.  Can be cast into shaped charges or mixed with scrap to pepper the blast area with high-velocity shrapnel."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "HMTD"
msgid_plural "HMTD"
msgstr[0] "HMTD"
msgstr[1] "HMTD"

#. ~ Description for HMTD
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Hexamine peroxide: this fine, yellowish powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, but best not store it for too long..."
msgstr "Hexamine peroxide: this fine, yellowish powder is a powerful primary explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as RDX.  Relatively stable, but best not store it for too long..."

#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid "rocket fuel"
msgid_plural "rocket fuel"
msgstr[0] "rocket fuel"
msgstr[1] "rocket fuel"

#. ~ Description for rocket fuel
#: lang/json/AMMO_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A chunk of a zinc powder and sulfur mixture, bound together by superglue, "
"that can be used as an impromptu rocket fuel."
msgstr "A chunk of a zinc powder and sulfur mixture, bound together by superglue, that can be used as an impromptu rocket fuel."

