msgstr[0] "blunderbuss"
msgstr[1] "blunderbusses"

#. ~ Description for blunderbuss
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A homemade version of a crude precursor to the shotgun.  Able to fire just "
"about anything you put down the barrel, but it will degrade pretty quick."
msgstr "A homemade version of a crude precursor to the shotgun.  Able to fire just about anything you put down the barrel, but it will degrade pretty quick."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "flamethrower"
msgid_plural "flamethrowers"
msgstr[0] "flamethrower"
msgstr[1] "flamethrowers"

#. ~ Description for flamethrower
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large flamethrower with substantial gas reserves.  Very menacing and "
"deadly."
msgstr "A large flamethrower with substantial gas reserves.  Very menacing and deadly."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "slosh."
msgstr "slosh."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "spraycan flamethrower"
msgid_plural "spraycan flamethrowers"
msgstr[0] "spraycan flamethrower"
msgstr[1] "spraycan flamethrowers"

#. ~ Description for spraycan flamethrower
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A favorite of hooligans around the world, this lighter duct-taped to a spray"
" can is probably as dangerous to the user as anyone else.  The nozzle has "
"been crudely modified to disperse gasoline, and a small pump attached to the"
" side allows for repressurization, though this process takes a few minutes."
msgstr "A favorite of hooligans around the world, this lighter duct-taped to a spray can is probably as dangerous to the user as anyone else.  The nozzle has been crudely modified to disperse gasoline, and a small pump attached to the side allows for repressurization, though this process takes a few minutes."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "simple flamethrower"
msgid_plural "simple flamethrowers"
msgstr[0] "simple flamethrower"
msgstr[1] "simple flamethrowers"

#. ~ Description for simple flamethrower
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A simple, home-made flamethrower.  While its capacity is not superb, it is "
"more than capable of igniting terrain and monsters alike."
msgstr "A simple, home-made flamethrower.  While its capacity is not superb, it is more than capable of igniting terrain and monsters alike."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "RM451 flamethrower"
msgid_plural "RM451 flamethrowers"
msgstr[0] "RM451 flamethrower"
msgstr[1] "RM451 flamethrowers"

#. ~ Description for RM451 flamethrower
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A military-grade combat flamethrower designed by Rivtech, the RM451 "
"flamethrower incorporates a cycling pressure rapid-feed fuel system with a "
"high-speed piezoelectric igniter.  Solidly built with durability in mind, it"
" serves as an incredibly destructive weapon in the right hands."
msgstr "A military-grade combat flamethrower designed by Rivtech, the RM451 flamethrower incorporates a cycling pressure rapid-feed fuel system with a high-speed piezoelectric igniter.  Solidly built with durability in mind, it serves as an incredibly destructive weapon in the right hands."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "flintlock carbine"
msgid_plural "flintlock carbines"
msgstr[0] "flintlock carbine"
msgstr[1] "flintlock carbines"

#. ~ Description for flintlock carbine
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This short rifle design once dominated the battlefields of ancient Europe, "
"and may yet re-earn its feared status due to its ease of handling and "
"ability to use easily-crafted ammunition."
msgstr "This short rifle design once dominated the battlefields of ancient Europe, and may yet re-earn its feared status due to its ease of handling and ability to use easily-crafted ammunition."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "double-barrel flintlock carbine"
msgid_plural "double-barrel flintlock carbines"
msgstr[0] "double-barrel flintlock carbine"
msgstr[1] "double-barrel flintlock carbines"

#. ~ Description for double-barrel flintlock carbine
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a compact muzzle-loading rifle combining a pair of rudimentary "
"flintlock actions and two barrels.  Whereas an antique multiple-barrel "
"flintlock is an intricate work of gunsmithing, this weapon is simpler yet "
"still serviceable."
msgstr "This is a compact muzzle-loading rifle combining a pair of rudimentary flintlock actions and two barrels.  Whereas an antique multiple-barrel flintlock is an intricate work of gunsmithing, this weapon is simpler yet still serviceable."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "flintlock pistol"
msgid_plural "flintlock pistols"
msgstr[0] "flintlock pistol"
msgstr[1] "flintlock pistols"

#. ~ Description for flintlock pistol
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A beautifully decorated flintlock pistol.  If using this doesn't makes you "
"feel a pirate, nothing will."
msgstr "A beautifully decorated flintlock pistol.  If using this doesn't makes you feel a pirate, nothing will."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "flintlock rifle"
msgid_plural "flintlock rifles"
msgstr[0] "flintlock rifle"
msgstr[1] "flintlock rifles"

#. ~ Description for flintlock rifle
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"For once, something *good* came back from the dead.  This ancient design "
"lacks the fire-rate of modern weapons, but packs as much punch as the best "
"of 'em and rewards the skilled shooter with easily-crafted ammunition."
msgstr "For once, something *good* came back from the dead.  This ancient design lacks the fire-rate of modern weapons, but packs as much punch as the best of 'em and rewards the skilled shooter with easily-crafted ammunition."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "heavy rail rifle"
msgid_plural "heavy rail rifles"
msgstr[0] "heavy rail rifle"
msgstr[1] "heavy rail rifles"

#. ~ Description for heavy rail rifle
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This overpowered and overengineered variant of the ferromagnetic rail rifle "
"was designed to deliver electromagnetically-driven obliteration right "
"through whatever obstacles that lies in front of it, be it buildings, "
"vehicles or hordes of walking dead.  However, the hefty bulk and weight of "
"this weapon compared to most contemporary rifles makes it somewhat "
"cumbersome to wield; not to mention that it consumes UPS charges at a "
"tremendous rate, making it impractical for use in prolonged engagements."
msgstr "This overpowered and overengineered variant of the ferromagnetic rail rifle was designed to deliver electromagnetically-driven obliteration right through whatever obstacles that lies in front of it, be it buildings, vehicles or hordes of walking dead.  However, the hefty bulk and weight of this weapon compared to most contemporary rifles makes it somewhat cumbersome to wield; not to mention that it consumes UPS charges at a tremendous rate, making it impractical for use in prolonged engagements."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "ferromagnetic rail rifle"
msgid_plural "ferromagnetic rail rifles"
msgstr[0] "ferromagnetic rail rifle"
msgstr[1] "ferromagnetic rail rifles"

#. ~ Description for ferromagnetic rail rifle
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A single-shot, electrically propelled, steel rail launcher handcrafted from "
"scrap.  The hypervelocity metal stake that it fires is accelerated to the "
"point of spontaneous combustion by a Lorentz force generated by "
"electromagnetic induction, powered by a standard UPS."
msgstr "A single-shot, electrically propelled, steel rail launcher handcrafted from scrap.  The hypervelocity metal stake that it fires is accelerated to the point of spontaneous combustion by a Lorentz force generated by electromagnetic induction, powered by a standard UPS."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "coilgun"
msgid_plural "coilguns"
msgstr[0] "coilgun"
msgstr[1] "coilguns"

#. ~ Description for coilgun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A homemade gun, using electromagnets to accelerate a ferromagnetic "
"projectile to high velocity.  Powered by UPS."
msgstr "A homemade gun, using electromagnets to accelerate a ferromagnetic projectile to high velocity.  Powered by UPS."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "nail gun"
msgid_plural "nail guns"
msgstr[0] "nail gun"
msgstr[1] "nail guns"

#. ~ Description for nail gun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A tool used to drive nails into wood or other material.  It could also be "
"used as a ad-hoc weapon."
msgstr "A tool used to drive nails into wood or other material.  It could also be used as a ad-hoc weapon."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "nail rifle"
msgid_plural "nail rifles"
msgstr[0] "nail rifle"
msgstr[1] "nail rifles"

#. ~ Description for nail rifle
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a nailgun that has been extensively modified with the addition of a "
"short barrel, stock and hand guard.  It can be reloaded using detachable "
"magazines and is an overall much more effective weapon."
msgstr "This is a nailgun that has been extensively modified with the addition of a short barrel, stock and hand guard.  It can be reloaded using detachable magazines and is an overall much more effective weapon."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "12 gauge pistol"
msgid_plural "12 gauge pistols"
msgstr[0] "12 gauge pistol"
msgstr[1] "12 gauge pistols"

#. ~ Description for 12 gauge pistol
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A single shot pistol that loads 12 gauge shotgun shells, handcrafted from "
"scrap."
msgstr "A single shot pistol that loads 12 gauge shotgun shells, handcrafted from scrap."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "manual autoshotgun"
msgid_plural "manual autoshotguns"
msgstr[0] "manual autoshotgun"
msgstr[1] "manual autoshotguns"

#. ~ Description for manual autoshotgun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A six-barrel hand-cranked automatic shotgun made from bicycle parts.  Though"
" a bit unwieldy, it is exceedingly powerful for such a simple machine."
msgstr "A six-barrel hand-cranked automatic shotgun made from bicycle parts.  Though a bit unwieldy, it is exceedingly powerful for such a simple machine."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "Kel-Tec KSG"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec KSG"
msgstr[0] "Kel-Tec KSG"
msgstr[1] "Kel-Tec KSG"

#. ~ Description for Kel-Tec KSG
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A bullpup pump-action shotgun, the Kel-Tec KSG uses a pair of magazine tubes"
" to increase its capacity.  Each tube has to be loaded separately, but this "
"offers the option of loading different ammunition for different situations."
msgstr "A bullpup pump-action shotgun, the Kel-Tec KSG uses a pair of magazine tubes to increase its capacity.  Each tube has to be loaded separately, but this offers the option of loading different ammunition for different situations."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "L12 Defender"
msgid_plural "L12 Defender"
msgstr[0] "L12 Defender"
msgstr[1] "L12 Defender"

#. ~ Description for L12 Defender
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Leadworks LLC's sole shotgun offering to date is surprisingly compact thanks"
" to its moving barrel and forward-back pump mechanism.  Like most other "
"Leadworks products it doesn't accept third-party modifications."
msgstr "Leadworks LLC's sole shotgun offering to date is surprisingly compact thanks to its moving barrel and forward-back pump mechanism.  Like most other Leadworks products it doesn't accept third-party modifications."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "M1014 shotgun"
msgid_plural "M1014 shotguns"
msgstr[0] "M1014 shotgun"
msgstr[1] "M1014 shotguns"

#. ~ Description for M1014 shotgun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Its relative simplicity and reliability made the Benelli M4 the most "
"successful semi-automatic shotgun ever created."
msgstr "Its relative simplicity and reliability made the Benelli M4 the most successful semi-automatic shotgun ever created."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "Mossberg 500"
msgid_plural "Mossberg 500"
msgstr[0] "Mossberg 500"
msgstr[1] "Mossberg 500"

#. ~ Description for Mossberg 500
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The Mossberg 500 is a popular series of pump-action shotguns, often acquired"
" for military use.  It is noted for its high durability and low recoil."
msgstr "The Mossberg 500 is a popular series of pump-action shotguns, often acquired for military use.  It is noted for its high durability and low recoil."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "double-barrel pipe shotgun"
msgid_plural "double-barrel pipe shotguns"
msgstr[0] "double-barrel pipe shotgun"
msgstr[1] "double-barrel pipe shotguns"

#. ~ Description for double-barrel pipe shotgun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A home-made double-barreled shotgun.  It is simply two pipes attached to a "
"stock, with a pair of hammers to strike the two rounds it holds."
msgstr "A home-made double-barreled shotgun.  It is simply two pipes attached to a stock, with a pair of hammers to strike the two rounds it holds."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "pipe shotgun"
msgid_plural "pipe shotguns"
msgstr[0] "pipe shotgun"
msgstr[1] "pipe shotguns"

#. ~ Description for pipe shotgun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A home-made shotgun.  It is simply a pipe attached to a stock, with a hammer"
" to strike the single round it holds."
msgstr "A home-made shotgun.  It is simply a pipe attached to a stock, with a hammer to strike the single round it holds."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "Remington 870"
msgid_plural "Remington 870"
msgstr[0] "Remington 870"
msgstr[1] "Remington 870"

#. ~ Description for Remington 870
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"One of the most popular shotguns on the market, the Remington 870 is used by"
" hunters and law enforcement agencies alike thanks to its high accuracy and "
"muzzle velocity."
msgstr "One of the most popular shotguns on the market, the Remington 870 is used by hunters and law enforcement agencies alike thanks to its high accuracy and muzzle velocity."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "shotgun revolver"
msgid_plural "shotgun revolvers"
msgstr[0] "shotgun revolver"
msgstr[1] "shotgun revolvers"

#. ~ Description for shotgun revolver
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A shotgun modified to use a revolver cylinder mechanism, it can hold 6 "
"cartridges."
msgstr "A shotgun modified to use a revolver cylinder mechanism, it can hold 6 cartridges."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "Saiga-12"
msgid_plural "Saiga-12s"
msgstr[0] "Saiga-12"
msgstr[1] "Saiga-12s"

#. ~ Description for Saiga-12
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The Saiga-12 is a semi-automatic shotgun designed on the same Kalashnikov "
"pattern as the AK47 rifle.  It reloads with a magazine, rather than one "
"shell at a time like most shotguns."
msgstr "The Saiga-12 is a semi-automatic shotgun designed on the same Kalashnikov pattern as the AK47 rifle.  It reloads with a magazine, rather than one shell at a time like most shotguns."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "double barrel shotgun"
msgid_plural "double barrel shotguns"
msgstr[0] "double barrel shotgun"
msgstr[1] "double barrel shotguns"

#. ~ Description for double barrel shotgun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An old shotgun, possibly antique.  It is little more than a pair of barrels,"
" a wood stock, and a hammer to strike the cartridges."
msgstr "An old shotgun, possibly antique.  It is little more than a pair of barrels, a wood stock, and a hammer to strike the cartridges."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "single barrel shotgun"
msgid_plural "single barrel shotguns"
msgstr[0] "single barrel shotgun"
msgstr[1] "single barrel shotguns"

#. ~ Description for single barrel shotgun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An old shotgun, possibly antique.  It is little more than a barrel, a wood "
"stock, and a hammer to strike the cartridge.  Its simple design keeps it "
"both light and accurate."
msgstr "An old shotgun, possibly antique.  It is little more than a barrel, a wood stock, and a hammer to strike the cartridge.  Its simple design keeps it both light and accurate."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift lever shotgun"
msgid_plural "makeshift lever shotguns"
msgstr[0] "makeshift lever shotgun"
msgstr[1] "makeshift lever shotguns"

#. ~ Description for makeshift lever shotgun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A well designed homemade lever-action shotgun.  With a 8 round magazine, "
"this is one of the better homemade weapons."
msgstr "A well designed homemade lever-action shotgun.  With a 8 round magazine, this is one of the better homemade weapons."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "flaregun"
msgid_plural "flareguns"
msgstr[0] "flaregun"
msgstr[1] "flareguns"

#. ~ Description for flaregun
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "A plastic single shot pistol that can be loaded with signal flares."
msgstr "A plastic single shot pistol that can be loaded with signal flares."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "XM34 EMP projector"
msgid_plural "XM34 EMP projectors"
msgstr[0] "XM34 EMP projector"
msgstr[1] "XM34 EMP projectors"

#. ~ Description for XM34 EMP projector
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A powerful electrolaser developed by the R&D outfit \"Aerial Labs\".  "
"Especially effective against electronic targets."
msgstr "A powerful electrolaser developed by the R&D outfit \"Aerial Labs\".  Especially effective against electronic targets."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "handheld laser cannon"
msgid_plural "handheld laser cannons"
msgstr[0] "handheld laser cannon"
msgstr[1] "handheld laser cannons"

#. ~ Description for handheld laser cannon
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a laser cannon stripped from the barrel of a TX-5LR Cerberus laser "
"turret that has been modified to use UPS power for firing."
msgstr "This is a laser cannon stripped from the barrel of a TX-5LR Cerberus laser turret that has been modified to use UPS power for firing."

#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid "A7 laser rifle"
msgid_plural "A7 laser rifles"
msgstr[0] "A7 laser rifle"
msgstr[1] "A7 laser rifles"

#. ~ Description for A7 laser rifle
#: lang/json/GUN_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A state of the art laser rifle developed by the R&D outfit \"Aerial Labs\"."
"  Initial performance rivaled Rivtech's finest, with rumors flying about "
"corporate skulduggery.  Though the cataclysm put that on the ash heap of "
"history, this weapon can still do the same to your foes."
