"This EMP grenade is active, and will shortly detonate, creating a large EMP "
"field that damages robots and drains bionic energy.  You may not want to be "
"holding it much longer."
msgstr "This EMP grenade is active, and will shortly detonate, creating a large EMP field that damages robots and drains bionic energy.  You may not want to be holding it much longer."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "packed M72 LAW"
msgid_plural "packed M72 LAWs"
msgstr[0] "packed M72 LAW"
msgstr[1] "packed M72 LAWs"

#. ~ Use action msg for packed M72 LAW.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You pull the activating lever, readying the LAW to fire."
msgstr "You pull the activating lever, readying the LAW to fire."

#. ~ Description for packed M72 LAW
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a M72 LAW, packed in its storage form.  Use it to pop it out and "
"make it ready to fire.  Once it is activated, it cannot be repacked."
msgstr "This is a M72 LAW, packed in its storage form.  Use it to pop it out and make it ready to fire.  Once it is activated, it cannot be repacked."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/ammunition_type_from_json.py
msgid "UPS"
msgid_plural "UPS's"
msgstr[0] "UPS"
msgstr[1] "UPS's"

#. ~ Description for UPS
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by"
" military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS"
" is designed to power armor and some guns, but drains batteries quickly."
msgstr "This is a unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS is designed to power armor and some guns, but drains batteries quickly."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "acid bomb"
msgid_plural "acid bombs"
msgstr[0] "acid bomb"
msgstr[1] "acid bombs"

#. ~ Description for acid bomb
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a fragile container filled with acid.  Throw it to spill out a pool "
"of potent acid."
msgstr "This is a fragile container filled with acid.  Throw it to spill out a pool of potent acid."

#. ~ Description for acid bomb
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a glass vial, with two chemicals mixing inside.  The vial feels "
"colder and the contents are frothing.  If this mixture is exposed to air (as"
" could happen if you throw the vial), it will spill out as a pool of potent "
"acid."
msgstr "This is a glass vial, with two chemicals mixing inside.  The vial feels colder and the contents are frothing.  If this mixture is exposed to air (as could happen if you throw the vial), it will spill out as a pool of potent acid."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "advanced UPS"
msgid_plural "advanced UPS's"
msgstr[0] "advanced UPS"
msgstr[1] "advanced UPS's"

#. ~ Description for advanced UPS
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an advanced version of the unified power supply, or UPS.  This "
"device has been significantly redesigned to provide better efficiency as "
"well as to consume plutonium fuel cells rather than batteries.  Sadly, its "
"plutonium reactor can't be charged in UPS charging station."
msgstr "This is an advanced version of the unified power supply, or UPS.  This device has been significantly redesigned to provide better efficiency as well as to consume plutonium fuel cells rather than batteries.  Sadly, its plutonium reactor can't be charged in UPS charging station."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "advanced electronic cigarette"
msgid_plural "advanced electronic cigarettes"
msgstr[0] "advanced electronic cigarette"
msgstr[1] "advanced electronic cigarettes"

#. ~ Description for advanced electronic cigarette
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An advanced version of the electronic cigarette.  A less harmful way to get "
"your nicotine fix than regular cigarettes, but still addictive.  It needs "
"batteries and nicotine liquid to function."
msgstr "An advanced version of the electronic cigarette.  A less harmful way to get your nicotine fix than regular cigarettes, but still addictive.  It needs batteries and nicotine liquid to function."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "compressed air horn"
msgid_plural "compressed air horns"
msgstr[0] "compressed air horn"
msgstr[1] "compressed air horns"

#. ~ Use action noise_message for compressed air horn.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "HOOOOONK!"
msgstr "HOOOOONK!"

#. ~ Description for compressed air horn
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small can of compressed air attached to a plastic horn.  Pressing "
"the button on top causes it to emit a loud honking sound."
msgstr "This is a small can of compressed air attached to a plastic horn.  Pressing the button on top causes it to emit a loud honking sound."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/furniture_from_json.py
msgid "anvil"
msgid_plural "anvils"
msgstr[0] "anvil"
msgstr[1] "anvils"

#. ~ Description for anvil
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an enormously heavy block of oddly shaped steel with a chisel-like "
"projection set into the corner.  It's used in most metalworking fabrication "
"recipes."
msgstr "This is an enormously heavy block of oddly shaped steel with a chisel-like projection set into the corner.  It's used in most metalworking fabrication recipes."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "wood axe"
msgid_plural "wood axes"
msgstr[0] "wood axe"
msgstr[1] "wood axes"

#. ~ Description for wood axe
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a large, two-handed wood axe.  It makes a good melee weapon, but is "
"a bit slow to recover between swings."
msgstr "This is a large, two-handed wood axe.  It makes a good melee weapon, but is a bit slow to recover between swings."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "banjo"
msgid_plural "banjos"
msgstr[0] "banjo"
msgstr[1] "banjos"

#. ~ Use action descriptions for banjo.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play a little tune on your banjo."
msgstr "You play a little tune on your banjo."

#. ~ Use action descriptions for banjo.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play a bluegrass tune on your banjo."
msgstr "You play a bluegrass tune on your banjo."

#. ~ Use action descriptions for banjo.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play a quick, Southern ditty on your banjo."
msgstr "You play a quick, Southern ditty on your banjo."

#. ~ Description for banjo
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "A standard factory-made banjo.  Looks to be in working condition."
msgstr "A standard factory-made banjo.  Looks to be in working condition."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "barometer"
msgid_plural "barometers"
msgstr[0] "barometer"
msgstr[1] "barometers"

#. ~ Description for barometer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "A plastic barometer that can read the atmospheric pressure."
msgstr "A plastic barometer that can read the atmospheric pressure."

#. ~ Description for battle axe
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a huge axe designed for warfare.  Though intended for use as a "
"weapon, it can also be pressed into service as a rather clumsy woodcutting "
"tool."
msgstr "This is a huge axe designed for warfare.  Though intended for use as a weapon, it can also be pressed into service as a rather clumsy woodcutting tool."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Louisville Slaughterer"
msgid_plural "Louisville Slaughterers"
msgstr[0] "Louisville Slaughterer"
msgstr[1] "Louisville Slaughterers"

#. ~ Use action msg for Louisville Slaughterer.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You light the Louisville Slaughterer."
msgstr "You light the Louisville Slaughterer."

#. ~ Description for Louisville Slaughterer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is sturdy wood bat, wrapped in gasoline-soaked rags and flame-resistant"
" Nomex fabric.  Light it, and the ball game will REALLY heat up.  You'll "
"need a lighter or matches to light it."
msgstr "This is sturdy wood bat, wrapped in gasoline-soaked rags and flame-resistant Nomex fabric.  Light it, and the ball game will REALLY heat up.  You'll need a lighter or matches to light it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py src/iuse.cpp
msgid "Louisville Slaughterer (lit)"
msgid_plural "Louisville Slaughterers (lit)"
msgstr[0] "Louisville Slaughterer (lit)"
msgstr[1] "Louisville Slaughterers (lit)"

#. ~ Description for Louisville Slaughterer (lit)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a sturdy wood bat, wrapped in gasoline-soaked rags and flame-"
"resistant Nomex fabric.  It is burning brightly, and makes it much easier to"
" see the baselines at night games (It also makes the umpire FAR more likely "
"to call a ball instead of a strike)."
msgstr "This is a sturdy wood bat, wrapped in gasoline-soaked rags and flame-resistant Nomex fabric.  It is burning brightly, and makes it much easier to see the baselines at night games (It also makes the umpire FAR more likely to call a ball instead of a strike)."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
msgid "bear trap"
msgid_plural "bear traps"
msgstr[0] "bear trap"
msgstr[1] "bear traps"

#. ~ Use action done_message for bear trap.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You set the beartrap."
msgstr "You set the beartrap."

#. ~ Use action bury_question for bear trap.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Bury the beartrap?"
msgstr "Bury the beartrap?"

#. ~ Use action done_message for bear trap.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You bury the beartrap."
msgstr "You bury the beartrap."

#. ~ Description for bear trap
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a spring-loaded pair of steel jaws connected to a sensitive pressure"
" plate.  Use it to set it on the ground, creating a trap that will ensnare "
"and damage anything that steps on it.  If you are carrying a shovel, you "
"will have the option of burying it."
msgstr "This is a spring-loaded pair of steel jaws connected to a sensitive pressure plate.  Use it to set it on the ground, creating a trap that will ensnare and damage anything that steps on it.  If you are carrying a shovel, you will have the option of burying it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "military black box"
msgid_plural "military black boxes"
msgstr[0] "military black box"
msgstr[1] "military black boxes"

#. ~ Description for military black box
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a black box, seemingly pulled from some sort of military vehicle "
"wreckage.  If you can find a system to analyze this you may find something "
"of interest."
msgstr "This is a black box, seemingly pulled from some sort of military vehicle wreckage.  If you can find a system to analyze this you may find something of interest."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "blade trap"
msgid_plural "blade traps"
msgstr[0] "blade trap"
msgstr[1] "blade traps"

#. ~ Use action done_message for blade trap.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You set the blade trap two squares away."
msgstr "You set the blade trap two squares away."

#. ~ Description for blade trap
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a machete attached laterally to a motor, with a tripwire controlling"
" its throttle.  When the tripwire is pulled, the blade is swung around with "
"great force.  The trap forms a 3x3 area of effect."
msgstr "This is a machete attached laterally to a motor, with a tripwire controlling its throttle.  When the tripwire is pulled, the blade is swung around with great force.  The trap forms a 3x3 area of effect."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "nailboard trap"
msgid_plural "nailboard traps"
msgstr[0] "nailboard trap"
msgstr[1] "nailboard traps"

#. ~ Use action done_message for nailboard trap.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#, no-python-format
msgid "You set the board trap on the %s, nails facing up."
msgstr "You set the board trap on the %s, nails facing up."

#. ~ Description for nailboard trap
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"These are several pieces of wood nailed together, with some nails sticking "
"straight up.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on it, they'll get nails "
"through the foot."
msgstr "These are several pieces of wood nailed together, with some nails sticking straight up.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on it, they'll get nails through the foot."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "pair of bolt cutters"
msgid_plural "pairs of bolt cutters"
msgstr[0] "pair of bolt cutters"
msgstr[1] "pairs of bolt cutters"

#. ~ Description for pair of bolt cutters
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a large pair of bolt cutters.  You could use them to cut padlocks or"
" heavy gauge wire."
msgstr "This is a large pair of bolt cutters.  You could use them to cut padlocks or heavy gauge wire."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
msgid "booby trap"
msgid_plural "booby traps"
msgstr[0] "booby trap"
msgstr[1] "booby traps"

#. ~ Use action done_message for booby trap.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You set the booby trap up and activate the grenade."
msgstr "You set the booby trap up and activate the grenade."

#. ~ Description for booby trap
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a crude explosive device triggered by a piece of string.  Use it to "
