"This is a combination of two Dark Age conflict-resolution classics, the "
"broadsword and the torch.  The blade is glowing with heat.  Excalibur can "
"eat its heart out.  Use to shut it off."
msgstr "This is a combination of two Dark Age conflict-resolution classics, the broadsword and the torch.  The blade is glowing with heat.  Excalibur can eat its heart out.  Use to shut it off."

#. ~ Description for broadsword
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an early modern sword seeing use in the 16th, 17th, and 18th "
"centuries.  Called 'broad' to contrast with the slimmer rapiers."
msgstr "This is an early modern sword seeing use in the 16th, 17th, and 18th centuries.  Called 'broad' to contrast with the slimmer rapiers."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
msgid "bubble wrap"
msgid_plural "bubble wraps"
msgstr[0] "bubble wrap"
msgstr[1] "bubble wraps"

#. ~ Use action done_message for bubble wrap.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You set the bubble wrap on the ground, ready to be popped."
msgstr "You set the bubble wrap on the ground, ready to be popped."

#. ~ Description for bubble wrap
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a sheet of plastic covered with air-filled bubbles.  Use it to set "
"it on the ground, creating a trap that will warn you with noise when "
"something steps on it."
msgstr "This is a sheet of plastic covered with air-filled bubbles.  Use it to set it on the ground, creating a trap that will warn you with noise when something steps on it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "C-4 explosive"
msgid_plural "C-4 explosives"
msgstr[0] "C-4 explosive"
msgstr[1] "C-4 explosives"

#. ~ Description for C-4 explosive
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is military grade RDX composition explosive.  A label reads: \"Highly "
"explosive, use with extreme caution!\" It comes with a small timer."
msgstr "This is military grade RDX composition explosive.  A label reads: \"Highly explosive, use with extreme caution!\" It comes with a small timer."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "C-4 explosive (armed)"
msgid_plural "C-4 explosives (armed)"
msgstr[0] "C-4 explosive (armed)"
msgstr[1] "C-4 explosives (armed)"

#. ~ Use action no_deactivate_msg for C-4 explosive (armed).
#. ~ Use action no_deactivate_msg for mininuke.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#, no-python-format
msgid "You've already set the %s's timer, you might want to get away from it."
msgstr "You've already set the %s's timer, you might want to get away from it."

#. ~ Description for C-4 explosive (armed)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is military grade RDX composition explosive.  A label reads: \"Highly "
"explosive, use with extreme caution!\" It comes with a small timer, which is"
" currently ticking down."
msgstr "This is military grade RDX composition explosive.  A label reads: \"Highly explosive, use with extreme caution!\" It comes with a small timer, which is currently ticking down."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "loose caltrops"
msgid_plural "loose caltrops"
msgstr[0] "loose caltrops"
msgstr[1] "loose caltrops"

#. ~ Use action done_message for loose caltrops.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#, no-python-format
msgid "You scatter the caltrops on the %s."
msgstr "You scatter the caltrops on the %s."

#. ~ Description for loose caltrops
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"These are small metal objects covered with many sharp points.  If an "
"unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get a spine through the foot."
msgstr "These are small metal objects covered with many sharp points.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get a spine through the foot."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "camera"
msgid_plural "cameras"
msgstr[0] "camera"
msgstr[1] "cameras"

#. ~ Description for camera
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A point-and-shoot digital camera, with digital viewfinder, a backup 'iron-"
"sight', and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen, or "
"transfer them with a memory card.  Takes conventional batteries."
msgstr "A point-and-shoot digital camera, with digital viewfinder, a backup 'iron-sight', and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen, or transfer them with a memory card.  Takes conventional batteries."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "camera pro"
msgid_plural "camera pros"
msgstr[0] "camera pro"
msgstr[1] "camera pros"

#. ~ Description for camera pro
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 35mm digital SLR (single-lens reflex) camera, with optical and digital "
"viewfinders, zoom lens with auto-focus and stabilizer, and flash.  You can "
"view your photos on it or transfer them with a memory card; it runs on "
"conventional batteries.  Before the cataclysm, you could have taken "
"professional-grade photos using this."
msgstr "A 35mm digital SLR (single-lens reflex) camera, with optical and digital viewfinders, zoom lens with auto-focus and stabilizer, and flash.  You can view your photos on it or transfer them with a memory card; it runs on conventional batteries.  Before the cataclysm, you could have taken professional-grade photos using this."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "candle"
msgid_plural "candles"
msgstr[0] "candle"
msgstr[1] "candles"

#. ~ Use action msg for candle.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You light the candle."
msgstr "You light the candle."

#. ~ Description for candle
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a thick candle.  It doesn't provide very much light, but it can burn"
" for quite a long time.  You'll need a lighter or matches to light it."
msgstr "This is a thick candle.  It doesn't provide very much light, but it can burn for quite a long time.  You'll need a lighter or matches to light it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "candle (lit)"
msgid_plural "candles (lit)"
msgstr[0] "candle (lit)"
msgstr[1] "candles (lit)"

#. ~ Use action msg for candle (lit).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The candle winks out."
msgstr "The candle winks out."

#. ~ Description for candle (lit)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a thick candle.  It doesn't provide very much light, but it can burn"
" for quite a long time.  This candle is lit."
msgstr "This is a thick candle.  It doesn't provide very much light, but it can burn for quite a long time.  This candle is lit."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "goo canister"
msgid_plural "goo canisters"
msgstr[0] "goo canister"
msgstr[1] "goo canisters"

#. ~ Description for goo canister
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"There is a label on this canister: \"Warning: contains highly toxic and "
"corrosive materials.  Contents may be sentient.  Open at your own risk.\" "
"You think you can feel something moving inside it."
msgstr "There is a label on this canister: \"Warning: contains highly toxic and corrosive materials.  Contents may be sentient.  Open at your own risk.\" You think you can feel something moving inside it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "electric carver (off)"
msgid_plural "electric carvers (off)"
msgstr[0] "electric carver (off)"
msgstr[1] "electric carvers (off)"

#. ~ Description for electric carver (off)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An electric meat carver powered by batteries.  Two serrated blades that "
"vibrate together to slice just about anything from turkey to ham...  even "
"zombies!"
msgstr "An electric meat carver powered by batteries.  Two serrated blades that vibrate together to slice just about anything from turkey to ham...  even zombies!"

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "electric carver (on)"
msgid_plural "electric carvers (on)"
msgstr[0] "electric carver (on)"
msgstr[1] "electric carvers (on)"

#. ~ Description for electric carver (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "This carver is on and the blades are buzzing.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr "This carver is on and the blades are buzzing.  Use it to turn it off."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "cat food"
msgid_plural "cat food"
msgstr[0] "cat food"
msgstr[1] "cat food"

#. ~ Description for cat food
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "This is food for cats.  It smells strange, but cats seem to love it."
msgstr "This is food for cats.  It smells strange, but cats seem to love it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "chainsaw (off)"
msgid_plural "chainsaws (off)"
msgstr[0] "chainsaw (off)"
msgstr[1] "chainsaws (off)"

#. ~ Description for chainsaw (off)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a lumbering tool moonlighting as weapon of opportunity.  If loaded "
"with gas, using this item will cause it to turn on, turning it into a very "
"powerful but unwieldy melee weapon."
msgstr "This is a lumbering tool moonlighting as weapon of opportunity.  If loaded with gas, using this item will cause it to turn on, turning it into a very powerful but unwieldy melee weapon."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "chainsaw (on)"
msgid_plural "chainsaws (on)"
msgstr[0] "chainsaw (on)"
msgstr[1] "chainsaws (on)"

#. ~ Description for chainsaw (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "This chainsaw is on and making a lot of noise.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr "This chainsaw is on and making a lot of noise.  Use it to turn it off."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "charcoal forge"
msgid_plural "charcoal forges"
msgstr[0] "charcoal forge"
msgstr[1] "charcoal forges"

#. ~ Description for charcoal forge
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a portable, charcoal fired, metalworking forge.  If combined with "
"the right tools, you could use this for metalworking."
msgstr "This is a portable, charcoal fired, metalworking forge.  If combined with the right tools, you could use this for metalworking."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "charcoal water purifier"
msgid_plural "charcoal water purifiers"
msgstr[0] "charcoal water purifier"
msgstr[1] "charcoal water purifiers"

#. ~ Description for charcoal water purifier
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Using this item on a container full of water will purify the water using "
"layered charcoal.  Once the charcoal has purified enough water, it will "
"become unusable and can be disassembled and recycled.  Water taken from "
"uncertain sources like a river may be dirty."
msgstr "Using this item on a container full of water will purify the water using layered charcoal.  Once the charcoal has purified enough water, it will become unusable and can be disassembled and recycled.  Water taken from uncertain sources like a river may be dirty."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "charcoal smoker"
msgid_plural "charcoal smokers"
msgstr[0] "charcoal smoker"
msgstr[1] "charcoal smokers"

#. ~ Description for charcoal smoker
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a portable charcoal smoker.  Good for weekend barbecuing and "
"preserving meat with smoke."
msgstr "This is a portable charcoal smoker.  Good for weekend barbecuing and preserving meat with smoke."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "charcoal cooker"
msgid_plural "charcoal cookers"
msgstr[0] "charcoal cooker"
msgstr[1] "charcoal cookers"

#. ~ Description for charcoal cooker
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a little metal tank for holding charcoal with a pilot light "
"attached.  You could use it for cooking food."
msgstr "This is a little metal tank for holding charcoal with a pilot light attached.  You could use it for cooking food."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "chemistry set"
msgid_plural "chemistry sets"
msgstr[0] "chemistry set"
msgstr[1] "chemistry sets"

#. ~ Description for chemistry set
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a chemistry set stored in a box.  The contents include glass "
"containers, hoses, metal wire, a hotplate, and safety glasses.  It might be "
"used to craft some chemistry projects if you're so inclined."
msgstr "This is a chemistry set stored in a box.  The contents include glass containers, hoses, metal wire, a hotplate, and safety glasses.  It might be used to craft some chemistry projects if you're so inclined."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "paint chipper"
msgid_plural "paint chippers"
msgstr[0] "paint chipper"
msgstr[1] "paint chippers"

#. ~ Description for paint chipper
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "A tool similar to a chisel, designed to remove paint."
msgstr "A tool similar to a chisel, designed to remove paint."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "metalworking chisel"
msgid_plural "metalworking chisels"
msgstr[0] "metalworking chisel"
msgstr[1] "metalworking chisels"

#. ~ Description for metalworking chisel
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a short, stout metalworking chisel.  It's used in some metalworking "
"fabrication recipes."
msgstr "This is a short, stout metalworking chisel.  It's used in some metalworking fabrication recipes."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "circular saw (off)"
msgid_plural "circular saws (off)"
msgstr[0] "circular saw (off)"
msgstr[1] "circular saws (off)"

#. ~ Use action msg for circular saw (off).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You turn on the circular saw."
msgstr "You turn on the circular saw."

#. ~ Description for circular saw (off)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A lightweight handheld cordless circular saw.  Spins a circular blade fast "
"enough to cut wood, metal, zombies, or in an emergency, pizza.  The blade, "
"while effective in combat, is hard to hit with due to its small size."
msgstr "A lightweight handheld cordless circular saw.  Spins a circular blade fast enough to cut wood, metal, zombies, or in an emergency, pizza.  The blade, while effective in combat, is hard to hit with due to its small size."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "circular saw (on)"
msgid_plural "circular saws (on)"
msgstr[0] "circular saw (on)"
msgstr[1] "circular saws (on)"

#. ~ Description for circular saw (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A lightweight handheld cordless circular saw.  It is currently on and the "
"blade is spinning; use this item to turn it off."
msgstr "A lightweight handheld cordless circular saw.  It is currently on and the blade is spinning; use this item to turn it off."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "clarinet"
msgid_plural "clarinets"
msgstr[0] "clarinet"
msgstr[1] "clarinets"

#. ~ Use action descriptions for clarinet.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play a little tune on your clarinet."
msgstr "You play a little tune on your clarinet."

#. ~ Use action descriptions for clarinet.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play a moving, orchestral piece on your clarinet."
msgstr "You play a moving, orchestral piece on your clarinet."

#. ~ Use action descriptions for clarinet.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play an uplifting marching tune on your clarinet."
msgstr "You play an uplifting marching tune on your clarinet."

#. ~ Description for clarinet
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "An ornate clarinet made from wood."
msgstr "An ornate clarinet made from wood."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "coffeemaker"
msgid_plural "coffeemakers"
msgstr[0] "coffeemaker"
msgstr[1] "coffeemakers"

#. ~ Description for coffeemaker
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a heating element with pot and frame for holding coffee or other "
"powders.  It's got a battery compartment for use when the power goes out.  "
"You can use it to make coffee, or other drinks if you so choose."
msgstr "This is a heating element with pot and frame for holding coffee or other powders.  It's got a battery compartment for use when the power goes out.  You can use it to make coffee, or other drinks if you so choose."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "combat chainsaw (off)"
msgid_plural "combat chainsaws (off)"
msgstr[0] "combat chainsaw (off)"
msgstr[1] "combat chainsaws (off)"

#. ~ Description for combat chainsaw (off)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a chainsaw that has been lightened, tuned, and extensively modified "
"to be a more effective weapon.  Unfortunately these modifications have "
"rendered it much less effective as a woodcutting tool."
msgstr "This is a chainsaw that has been lightened, tuned, and extensively modified to be a more effective weapon.  Unfortunately these modifications have rendered it much less effective as a woodcutting tool."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "combat chainsaw (on)"
msgid_plural "combat chainsaws (on)"
msgstr[0] "combat chainsaw (on)"
msgstr[1] "combat chainsaws (on)"

#. ~ Description for combat chainsaw (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This combat chainsaw is on, and is continuously draining gasoline.  Use it "
"to turn it off."
msgstr "This combat chainsaw is on, and is continuously draining gasoline.  Use it to turn it off."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "concrete mixer"
msgid_plural "concrete mixers"
msgstr[0] "concrete mixer"
msgstr[1] "concrete mixers"

#. ~ Description for concrete mixer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A portable concrete mixer.  It is still large and heavy, but it can be "
"operated solo, and runs on batteries.  It also has a heater built in."
msgstr "A portable concrete mixer.  It is still large and heavy, but it can be operated solo, and runs on batteries.  It also has a heater built in."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "control laptop"
msgid_plural "control laptops"
msgstr[0] "control laptop"
msgstr[1] "control laptops"

#. ~ Description for control laptop
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A modified laptop, now capable of transmitting in the ultra high frequencies"
" utilized by robots.  Activate it to command robots from afar."
msgstr "A modified laptop, now capable of transmitting in the ultra high frequencies utilized by robots.  Activate it to command robots from afar."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "copper axe"
msgid_plural "copper axes"
msgstr[0] "copper axe"
msgstr[1] "copper axes"

#. ~ Description for copper axe
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a decent-sized chunk of worked copper affixed to a wooden shaft, to "
"make a crude yet effective axe."
msgstr "This is a decent-sized chunk of worked copper affixed to a wooden shaft, to make a crude yet effective axe."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "copper knife"
msgid_plural "copper knives"
msgstr[0] "copper knife"
msgstr[1] "copper knives"

#. ~ Description for copper knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A knife consisting of crudely-worked copper, and a simple handle.  "
"Primitive, but a step above stone-age."
msgstr "A knife consisting of crudely-worked copper, and a simple handle.  Primitive, but a step above stone-age."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "cordless drill"
msgid_plural "cordless drills"
msgstr[0] "cordless drill"
msgstr[1] "cordless drills"

#. ~ Description for cordless drill
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a cordless battery-powered drill with a selection of drill bits."
msgstr "This is a cordless battery-powered drill with a selection of drill bits."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
msgid "cot"
msgid_plural "cots"
msgstr[0] "cot"
msgstr[1] "cots"

#. ~ Use action done_message for cot.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You unfold the cot and place it on the ground."
msgstr "You unfold the cot and place it on the ground."

#. ~ Description for cot
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a military style fold up cot.  While it may not be quite as "
"comfortable as a bed, it's better than slumming it on the ground."
msgstr "This is a military style fold up cot.  While it may not be quite as comfortable as a bed, it's better than slumming it on the ground."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "cow bell"
msgid_plural "cow bells"
msgstr[0] "cow bell"
msgstr[1] "cow bells"

#. ~ Description for cow bell
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "A brass cow bell.  Potentially useful in so many ways."
msgstr "A brass cow bell.  Potentially useful in so many ways."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "crack pipe"
msgid_plural "crack pipes"
msgstr[0] "crack pipe"
msgstr[1] "crack pipes"

#. ~ Description for crack pipe
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a fine glass tube with a bulb with a bowl on one end.  It's used to "
"partake of certain illicit substances."
msgstr "This is a fine glass tube with a bulb with a bowl on one end.  It's used to partake of certain illicit substances."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "talking doll"
msgid_plural "talking dolls"
msgstr[0] "talking doll"
msgstr[1] "talking dolls"

#. ~ Description for talking doll
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a talking doll, meant for children.  Fortunately it still works, and"
" you could unload the batteries out of it."
msgstr "This is a talking doll, meant for children.  Fortunately it still works, and you could unload the batteries out of it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
msgid "crossbow trap"
msgid_plural "crossbow traps"
msgstr[0] "crossbow trap"
msgstr[1] "crossbow traps"

#. ~ Use action done_message for crossbow trap.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You set the crossbow trap."
msgstr "You set the crossbow trap."

#. ~ Description for crossbow trap
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a simple tripwire, which is attached to the trigger of a loaded "
"crossbow.  When pulled, the crossbow fires.  Only a single round can be "
"used, after which the trap is disabled."
msgstr "This is a simple tripwire, which is attached to the trigger of a loaded crossbow.  When pulled, the crossbow fires.  Only a single round can be used, after which the trap is disabled."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "crowbar"
msgid_plural "crowbars"
msgstr[0] "crowbar"
msgstr[1] "crowbars"

#. ~ Description for crowbar
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hefty prying tool.  Use it to open locked doors without destroying"
" them or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash some heads"
" in."
msgstr "This is a hefty prying tool.  Use it to open locked doors without destroying them or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash some heads in."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "crucible"
msgid_plural "crucibles"
msgstr[0] "crucible"
msgstr[1] "crucibles"

#. ~ Description for crucible
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small metalworking crucible.  It's used in some metalworking "
"fabrication recipes."
msgstr "This is a small metalworking crucible.  It's used in some metalworking fabrication recipes."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "clay crucible"
msgid_plural "clay crucibles"
msgstr[0] "clay crucible"
msgstr[1] "clay crucibles"

#. ~ Description for clay crucible
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a primitive metalworking crucible made of clay.  You could use it "
"for metalworking."
msgstr "This is a primitive metalworking crucible made of clay.  You could use it for metalworking."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "electric firestarter"
msgid_plural "electric firestarters"
msgstr[0] "electric firestarter"
msgstr[1] "electric firestarters"

#. ~ Description for electric firestarter
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a crudely made electric firestarter, which can function as an "
"inefficient lighter."
msgstr "This is a crudely made electric firestarter, which can function as an inefficient lighter."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "improvised lockpick"
msgid_plural "improvised lockpicks"
msgstr[0] "improvised lockpick"
msgstr[1] "improvised lockpicks"

#. ~ Description for improvised lockpick
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an improvised set of picks and torsion wrenches made from scrap "
"metal.  You need MacGyver-like skills to open locks with these as they are "
"brittle, but they lower the chances of alarms being set off."
