msgid "flammable arrow"
msgid_plural "flammable arrows"
msgstr[0] "flammable arrow"
msgstr[1] "flammable arrows"

#. ~ Description for flammable arrow
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This arrow has a rag soaked in a flammable liquid wrapped around the shaft "
"near the head.  You need to light it before shooting."
msgstr "This arrow has a rag soaked in a flammable liquid wrapped around the shaft near the head.  You need to light it before shooting."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "flashbang"
msgid_plural "flashbangs"
msgstr[0] "flashbang"
msgstr[1] "flashbangs"

#. ~ Use action msg for flashbang.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You pull the pin on the flashbang."
msgstr "You pull the pin on the flashbang."

#. ~ Description for flashbang
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a military police style flashbang.  Use this item to pull the pin "
"and light the fuse.  You will then have five turns before it detonates with "
"intense light and sound, blinding, deafening and disorienting anyone nearby."
msgstr "This is a military police style flashbang.  Use this item to pull the pin and light the fuse.  You will then have five turns before it detonates with intense light and sound, blinding, deafening and disorienting anyone nearby."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "active flashbang"
msgid_plural "active flashbangs"
msgstr[0] "active flashbang"
msgstr[1] "active flashbangs"

#. ~ Description for active flashbang
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This flashbang is active, and will soon detonate with intense light and "
"sound, blinding, deafening and disorienting anyone nearby.  It may be a good"
" idea to throw it!"
msgstr "This flashbang is active, and will soon detonate with intense light and sound, blinding, deafening and disorienting anyone nearby.  It may be a good idea to throw it!"

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "flute"
msgid_plural "flutes"
msgstr[0] "flute"
msgstr[1] "flutes"

#. ~ Use action descriptions for flute.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play a little tune on your flute."
msgstr "You play a little tune on your flute."

#. ~ Use action descriptions for flute.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play a beautiful piece on your flute."
msgstr "You play a beautiful piece on your flute."

#. ~ Use action descriptions for flute.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You play a piece on your flute that sounds harmonious with nature."
msgstr "You play a piece on your flute that sounds harmonious with nature."

#. ~ Description for flute
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "A simple silver-plated flute."
msgstr "A simple silver-plated flute."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "folding bicycle"
msgid_plural "folding bicycles"
msgstr[0] "folding bicycle"
msgstr[1] "folding bicycles"

#. ~ Use action unfold_msg for folding bicycle.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You painstakingly unfold the bicycle and make it ready to ride."
msgstr "You painstakingly unfold the bicycle and make it ready to ride."

#. ~ Description for folding bicycle
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "This is a bicycle folded into a relatively portable package."
msgstr "This is a bicycle folded into a relatively portable package."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "electric forge"
msgid_plural "electric forges"
msgstr[0] "electric forge"
msgstr[1] "electric forges"

#. ~ Description for electric forge
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a portable electric metalworking forge, powered by batteries.  "
"Combined with the right tools, you could use this for metalworking.  With a "
"little mechanical know-how, you could probably even convert it to run "
"directly off a vehicle's power system."
msgstr "This is a portable electric metalworking forge, powered by batteries.  Combined with the right tools, you could use this for metalworking.  With a little mechanical know-how, you could probably even convert it to run directly off a vehicle's power system."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "funnel"
msgid_plural "funnels"
msgstr[0] "funnel"
msgstr[1] "funnels"

#. ~ Use action done_message for funnel.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You place the funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "You place the funnel, waiting to collect rain."

#. ~ Description for funnel
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside and place a "
"container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr "This is a funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "fur rollmat"
msgid_plural "fur rollmats"
msgstr[0] "fur rollmat"
msgstr[1] "fur rollmats"

#. ~ Use action done_message for fur rollmat.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You unroll the fur mat and lay it on the ground."
msgstr "You unroll the fur mat and lay it on the ground."

#. ~ Description for fur rollmat
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a bedroll made of pelts which can be rolled up for transport.  It "
"insulates you from the floor, making it easier to sleep.  Use it to unroll "
"and place on the ground."
msgstr "This is a bedroll made of pelts which can be rolled up for transport.  It insulates you from the floor, making it easier to sleep.  Use it to unroll and place on the ground."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "trowel"
msgid_plural "trowels"
msgstr[0] "trowel"
msgstr[1] "trowels"

#. ~ Description for trowel
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small, sharp gardening shovel, perfect for digging up grubs and worms."
msgstr "A small, sharp gardening shovel, perfect for digging up grubs and worms."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift gas canister"
msgid_plural "makeshift gas canisters"
msgstr[0] "makeshift gas canister"
msgstr[1] "makeshift gas canisters"

#. ~ Use action msg for makeshift gas canister.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You arm the makeshift gas canister."
msgstr "You arm the makeshift gas canister."

#. ~ Description for makeshift gas canister
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a crude gasbomb using household chemicals.  Use this item to arm it."
"  In three turns it will begin to expel a highly toxic gas for a short time."
"  This gas poisons those exposed to it, in addition to obscuring vision and "
"scent."
msgstr "This is a crude gasbomb using household chemicals.  Use this item to arm it.  In three turns it will begin to expel a highly toxic gas for a short time.  This gas poisons those exposed to it, in addition to obscuring vision and scent."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "active makeshift gas grenade"
msgid_plural "active makeshift gas grenades"
msgstr[0] "active makeshift gas grenade"
msgstr[1] "active makeshift gas grenades"

#. ~ Use action sound_msg for active makeshift gas grenade.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Hiss."
msgstr "Hiss."

#. ~ Use action no_deactivate_msg for active makeshift gas grenade.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#, no-python-format
msgid "You've already armed the %s, try throwing it instead."
msgstr "You've already armed the %s, try throwing it instead."

#. ~ Description for active makeshift gas grenade
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This homemade canister of poison gas has been unsealed, and is (or will "
"shortly be) expelling highly toxic gas.  You should consider getting rid of "
"it soon."
msgstr "This homemade canister of poison gas has been unsealed, and is (or will shortly be) expelling highly toxic gas.  You should consider getting rid of it soon."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "gasoline cooker"
msgid_plural "gasoline cookers"
msgstr[0] "gasoline cooker"
msgstr[1] "gasoline cookers"

#. ~ Description for gasoline cooker
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a simple heater powered by gasoline.  It is designed for cooking "
"food."
msgstr "This is a simple heater powered by gasoline.  It is designed for cooking food."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "gasoline lantern (off)"
msgid_plural "gasoline lanterns (off)"
msgstr[0] "gasoline lantern (off)"
msgstr[1] "gasoline lanterns (off)"

#. ~ Use action msg for gasoline lantern (off).
#. ~ Use action msg for oil lamp (off).
#. ~ Use action msg for electric lantern (off).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You turn the lamp on."
msgstr "You turn the lamp on."

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for gasoline lantern (off).
#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for oil lamp (off).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The lamp is empty."
msgstr "The lamp is empty."

#. ~ Description for gasoline lantern (off)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small gasoline powered lantern.  It does not provide much light, "
"but it lasts a long time.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr "This is a small gasoline powered lantern.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  Use it to turn it on."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "gasoline lantern (on)"
msgid_plural "gasoline lanterns (on)"
msgstr[0] "gasoline lantern (on)"
msgstr[1] "gasoline lanterns (on)"

#. ~ Use action msg for gasoline lantern (on).
#. ~ Use action msg for oil lamp (on).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The lantern is extinguished."
msgstr "The lantern is extinguished."

#. ~ Description for gasoline lantern (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small gasoline powered lantern.  It does not provide much light, "
"but it lasts a long time.  It is turned on.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr "This is a small gasoline powered lantern.  It does not provide much light, but it lasts a long time.  It is turned on.  Use it to turn it off."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "geiger counter (off)"
msgid_plural "geiger counters (off)"
msgstr[0] "geiger counter (off)"
msgstr[1] "geiger counters (off)"

#. ~ Description for geiger counter (off)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a tool for measuring radiation.  Using it will prompt you to choose "
"whether to scan yourself or the terrain, or to turn it on, which will "
"provide continuous feedback on ambient radiation.  It is currently off."
msgstr "This is a tool for measuring radiation.  Using it will prompt you to choose whether to scan yourself or the terrain, or to turn it on, which will provide continuous feedback on ambient radiation.  It is currently off."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "geiger counter (on)"
msgid_plural "geiger counters (on)"
msgstr[0] "geiger counter (on)"
msgstr[1] "geiger counters (on)"

#. ~ Description for geiger counter (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a tool for measuring radiation.  It is in continuous scan mode, and "
"will produce quiet clicking sounds in the presence of ambient radiation.  "
"Using it allows you to turn it off, or scan yourself or the ground.  It is "
"currently on."
msgstr "This is a tool for measuring radiation.  It is in continuous scan mode, and will produce quiet clicking sounds in the presence of ambient radiation.  Using it allows you to turn it off, or scan yourself or the ground.  It is currently on."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glowstick"
msgid_plural "glowsticks"
msgstr[0] "glowstick"
msgstr[1] "glowsticks"

#. ~ Use action msg for glowstick.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You activate the glowstick."
msgstr "You activate the glowstick."

#. ~ Description for glowstick
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small blue light glowstick.  Use it to bend the plastic and break "
"the glass cylinder inside to start the reaction.  It will produce a small "
"amount of light."
msgstr "This is a small blue light glowstick.  Use it to bend the plastic and break the glass cylinder inside to start the reaction.  It will produce a small amount of light."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "dead glowstick"
msgid_plural "dead glowsticks"
msgstr[0] "dead glowstick"
msgstr[1] "dead glowsticks"

#. ~ Description for dead glowstick
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "This is a spent glowstick.  It is essentially trash."
msgstr "This is a spent glowstick.  It is essentially trash."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "active glowstick"
msgid_plural "active glowsticks"
msgstr[0] "active glowstick"
msgstr[1] "active glowsticks"

#. ~ Description for active glowstick
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an active glowstick and is producing light.  It will last for a few "
"hours before burning out."
msgstr "This is an active glowstick and is producing light.  It will last for a few hours before burning out."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "grenade"
msgid_plural "grenades"
msgstr[0] "grenade"
msgstr[1] "grenades"

#. ~ Use action msg for grenade.
#. ~ Use action msg for incendiary grenade.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You pull the pin on the grenade."
msgstr "You pull the pin on the grenade."

#. ~ Description for grenade
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a military grade fragmentary hand grenade.  Use this item to pull "
"the pin and light the fuse.  You will then have five turns before it "
"explodes; throwing it would be a good idea."
msgstr "This is a military grade fragmentary hand grenade.  Use this item to pull the pin and light the fuse.  You will then have five turns before it explodes; throwing it would be a good idea."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "active grenade"
msgid_plural "active grenades"
msgstr[0] "active grenade"
msgstr[1] "active grenades"

#. ~ Description for active grenade
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an active grenade, and will explode any second now.  Better throw "
"it!"
msgstr "This is an active grenade, and will explode any second now.  Better throw it!"

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "incendiary grenade"
msgid_plural "incendiary grenades"
msgstr[0] "incendiary grenade"
msgstr[1] "incendiary grenades"

#. ~ Description for incendiary grenade
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a military grade incendiary hand grenade.  Use this item to pull the"
" pin and light the fuse.  You will then have five turns before it explodes "
"into a raging inferno; throwing it would be a good idea."
msgstr "This is a military grade incendiary hand grenade.  Use this item to pull the pin and light the fuse.  You will then have five turns before it explodes into a raging inferno; throwing it would be a good idea."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "active incendiary grenade"
msgid_plural "active incendiary grenades"
msgstr[0] "active incendiary grenade"
msgstr[1] "active incendiary grenades"

#. ~ Description for active incendiary grenade
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an active incendiary grenade, likely to burst into an inferno any "
"second now.  Better throw it!"
msgstr "This is an active incendiary grenade, likely to burst into an inferno any second now.  Better throw it!"

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "hacksaw"
msgid_plural "hacksaws"
msgstr[0] "hacksaw"
msgstr[1] "hacksaws"

#. ~ Description for hacksaw
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "This is a sturdy saw, useful for cutting through metal objects."
msgstr "This is a sturdy saw, useful for cutting through metal objects."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Halligan bar"
msgid_plural "Halligan bars"
msgstr[0] "Halligan bar"
msgstr[1] "Halligan bars"

#. ~ Description for Halligan bar
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a heavy multiple-use tool commonly carried by firefighters, law "
"enforcement, and military rescue units.  Use it to open locked doors without"
" destroying them or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash"
" some heads in."
msgstr "This is a heavy multiple-use tool commonly carried by firefighters, law enforcement, and military rescue units.  Use it to open locked doors without destroying them or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash some heads in."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "hammer"
msgid_plural "hammers"
msgstr[0] "hammer"
msgstr[1] "hammers"

#. ~ Description for hammer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a demagnetized steel hammer with a wooden grip.  With a hammer, "
"nails, and two by fours in your inventory, you could board up adjacent doors"
" and windows.  It has myriad other uses as well."
msgstr "This is a demagnetized steel hammer with a wooden grip.  With a hammer, nails, and two by fours in your inventory, you could board up adjacent doors and windows.  It has myriad other uses as well."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "hand drill"
msgid_plural "hand drills"
msgstr[0] "hand drill"
msgstr[1] "hand drills"

#. ~ Description for hand drill
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A primitive manual drill with a single drill bit.  It is slow and it will "
"exhaust you quickly."
msgstr "A primitive manual drill with a single drill bit.  It is slow and it will exhaust you quickly."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "heat pack"
msgid_plural "heat packs"
msgstr[0] "heat pack"
msgstr[1] "heat packs"

#. ~ Description for heat pack
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a chemical heat pack.  It's used to treat sports injuries and heat "
"food.  It is usable only once."
msgstr "This is a chemical heat pack.  It's used to treat sports injuries and heat food.  It is usable only once."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "used heat pack"
msgid_plural "used heat packs"
msgstr[0] "used heat pack"
msgstr[1] "used heat packs"

#. ~ Description for used heat pack
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a chemical heat pack.  It's used to treat sports injuries and heat "
"food.  This one has been used and is chemically inert, rendering it useless."
msgstr "This is a chemical heat pack.  It's used to treat sports injuries and heat food.  This one has been used and is chemically inert, rendering it useless."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "heavy snare kit"
msgid_plural "heavy snare kits"
msgstr[0] "heavy snare kit"
msgstr[1] "heavy snare kits"

#. ~ Use action done_message for heavy snare kit.
#. ~ Use action done_message for light snare kit.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You set the snare trap."
msgstr "You set the snare trap."

#. ~ Description for heavy snare kit
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a kit for a simple trap consisting of a rope noose and a snare "
"trigger.  It requires a tree nearby.  It is effective at trapping monsters."
msgstr "This is a kit for a simple trap consisting of a rope noose and a snare trigger.  It requires a tree nearby.  It is effective at trapping monsters."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "hoe"
msgid_plural "hoes"
msgstr[0] "hoe"
msgstr[1] "hoes"

#. ~ Description for hoe
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a farming implement.  Use it to turn tillable land into a slow-to-"
"cross pile of dirt."
msgstr "This is a farming implement.  Use it to turn tillable land into a slow-to-cross pile of dirt."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "honey scraper"
msgid_plural "honey scrapers"
msgstr[0] "honey scraper"
msgstr[1] "honey scrapers"

#. ~ Description for honey scraper
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sharp, knife-like tool used in harvesting honey from beehives.  Makes a "
"passable melee weapon."
msgstr "A sharp, knife-like tool used in harvesting honey from beehives.  Makes a passable melee weapon."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "bicycle horn"
msgid_plural "bicycle horns"
msgstr[0] "bicycle horn"
msgstr[1] "bicycle horns"

#. ~ Weak horn sound
#. ~ Use action noise_message for bicycle horn.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py src/vehicle.cpp
msgid "honk."
msgstr "honk."

#. ~ Description for bicycle horn
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a simple bulb horn, found on many bicycles.  Use to honk.  Honk "
"honk."
msgstr "This is a simple bulb horn, found on many bicycles.  Use to honk.  Honk honk."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "truck horn"
msgid_plural "truck horns"
msgstr[0] "truck horn"
msgstr[1] "truck horns"

#. ~ Description for truck horn
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "This is a very loud horn, usually found on large trucks like semis."
msgstr "This is a very loud horn, usually found on large trucks like semis."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "car horn"
msgid_plural "car horns"
msgstr[0] "car horn"
msgstr[1] "car horns"

#. ~ Description for car horn
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "This is a car horn meant to be attached to a car's electrical system."
msgstr "This is a car horn meant to be attached to a car's electrical system."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "rubber hose"
msgid_plural "rubber hoses"
msgstr[0] "rubber hose"
msgstr[1] "rubber hoses"

#. ~ Description for rubber hose
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a flexible rubber hose.  It could be used for crafting, or siphoning"
" fuel from a vehicle."
msgstr "This is a flexible rubber hose.  It could be used for crafting, or siphoning fuel from a vehicle."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "hotplate"
msgid_plural "hotplates"
msgstr[0] "hotplate"
msgstr[1] "hotplates"

#. ~ Description for hotplate
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small heating element on a stand, powered by batteries.  It is "
"indispensable for cooking and chemistry.  Try not to burn yourself."
msgstr "This is a small heating element on a stand, powered by batteries.  It is indispensable for cooking and chemistry.  Try not to burn yourself."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "hygrometer"
msgid_plural "hygrometers"
msgstr[0] "hygrometer"
msgstr[1] "hygrometers"

#. ~ Description for hygrometer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "A plastic hygrometer that can read the relative humidity in the air."
msgstr "A plastic hygrometer that can read the relative humidity in the air."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "ice axe"
msgid_plural "ice axes"
msgstr[0] "ice axe"
msgstr[1] "ice axes"

#. ~ Description for ice axe
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an ice axe with hammer on its head, a multi-purpose hiking and "
"climbing tool used by mountaineers.  It is sturdy enough, so you can use it "
"to pry open closed doors or lift manhole covers."
msgstr "This is an ice axe with hammer on its head, a multi-purpose hiking and climbing tool used by mountaineers.  It is sturdy enough, so you can use it to pry open closed doors or lift manhole covers."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "jackhammer"
msgid_plural "jackhammers"
msgstr[0] "jackhammer"
msgstr[1] "jackhammers"

#. ~ Description for jackhammer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a construction tool for drilling through hard rock or other "
"surfaces.  It runs on gasoline.  Use it (if loaded) to blast a hole in "
"adjacent solid terrain."
msgstr "This is a construction tool for drilling through hard rock or other surfaces.  It runs on gasoline.  Use it (if loaded) to blast a hole in adjacent solid terrain."

#. ~ Description for katana
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a rare sword from Japan.  Deadly against unarmored targets, and "
"still very effective against armor."
msgstr "This is a rare sword from Japan.  Deadly against unarmored targets, and still very effective against armor."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Kevlar plate"
msgid_plural "Kevlar plates"
msgstr[0] "Kevlar plate"
msgstr[1] "Kevlar plates"

#. ~ Description for Kevlar plate
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a plate of reinforced Kevlar.  It could be used to repair items made"
" of Kevlar."
msgstr "This is a plate of reinforced Kevlar.  It could be used to repair items made of Kevlar."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "finished charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "finished charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "finished charcoal kiln"
msgstr[1] "finished charcoal kilns"

#. ~ Description for finished charcoal kiln
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A charcoal kiln that has finished burning.  Disassemble it to retrieve the "
"charcoal and kiln."
msgstr "A charcoal kiln that has finished burning.  Disassemble it to retrieve the charcoal and kiln."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/furniture_from_json.py
msgid "filled charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "filled charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "filled charcoal kiln"
msgstr[1] "filled charcoal kilns"

#. ~ Use action need_fire_msg for filled charcoal kiln.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You need something to light it with!"
msgstr "You need something to light it with!"

#. ~ Use action msg for filled charcoal kiln.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You light the wood."
msgstr "You light the wood."

#. ~ Description for filled charcoal kiln
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A kiln filled with wood which will become charcoal after a slow period of "
"burning."
msgstr "A kiln filled with wood which will become charcoal after a slow period of burning."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "butcher knife"
msgid_plural "butcher knives"
msgstr[0] "butcher knife"
msgstr[1] "butcher knives"

#. ~ Description for butcher knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a sharp, heavy knife.  It makes a good melee weapon, and is an ideal"
" item for butchering corpses."
msgstr "This is a sharp, heavy knife.  It makes a good melee weapon, and is an ideal item for butchering corpses."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "combat knife"
msgid_plural "combat knives"
msgstr[0] "combat knife"
msgstr[1] "combat knives"

#. ~ Description for combat knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a military combat knife.  It is light and extremely sharp, and could"
" be deadly in either the right hands or when attached as a bayonet."
msgstr "This is a military combat knife.  It is light and extremely sharp, and could be deadly in either the right hands or when attached as a bayonet."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "hunting knife"
msgid_plural "hunting knives"
msgstr[0] "hunting knife"
msgstr[1] "hunting knives"

#. ~ Description for hunting knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Commonly used by hunters, this single-edge sheath knife is designed for "
"cutting and skinning game rather than combat."
msgstr "Commonly used by hunters, this single-edge sheath knife is designed for cutting and skinning game rather than combat."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "survival knife"
msgid_plural "survival knives"
msgstr[0] "survival knife"
msgstr[1] "survival knives"

#. ~ Description for survival knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This massive knife features a hollow handle with a compass built into the "
"pommel and a row of fearsome looking saw teeth along the back of its blade."
msgstr "This massive knife features a hollow handle with a compass built into the pommel and a row of fearsome looking saw teeth along the back of its blade."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "RM42 fighting knife"
msgid_plural "RM42 fighting knives"
msgstr[0] "RM42 fighting knife"
msgstr[1] "RM42 fighting knives"

#. ~ Description for RM42 fighting knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This sturdy matte black Rivtech combat dagger features a long and slim "
"double-edged blade with a spear-point and a distinctive slip-resistant grip "
"which can also be used to affix it to a suitable firearm.  Originally "
"manufactured for the military, it was very popular in films and among "
"collectors due to its fearsome appearance."
msgstr "This sturdy matte black Rivtech combat dagger features a long and slim double-edged blade with a spear-point and a distinctive slip-resistant grip which can also be used to affix it to a suitable firearm.  Originally manufactured for the military, it was very popular in films and among collectors due to its fearsome appearance."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "steak knife"
msgid_plural "steak knives"
msgstr[0] "steak knife"
msgstr[1] "steak knives"

#. ~ Description for steak knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a sharp knife, designed for cutting meat.  It makes a poor melee "
"weapon, but is decent at butchering corpses."
msgstr "This is a sharp knife, designed for cutting meat.  It makes a poor melee weapon, but is decent at butchering corpses."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Swiss Army knife"
msgid_plural "Swiss Army knives"
msgstr[0] "Swiss Army knife"
msgstr[1] "Swiss Army knives"

#. ~ Description for Swiss Army knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An iconic pocket knife imported from Europe.  Its red plastic handle "
"conceals many small tools."
msgstr "An iconic pocket knife imported from Europe.  Its red plastic handle conceals many small tools."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "trench knife"
msgid_plural "trench knives"
msgstr[0] "trench knife"
msgstr[1] "trench knives"

#. ~ Description for trench knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This stout combat knife features a steel guard to protect the user's "
"knuckles.  The guard can also be used for striking or blocking, and the "
"knife can also be used to butcher corpses."
msgstr "This stout combat knife features a steel guard to protect the user's knuckles.  The guard can also be used for striking or blocking, and the knife can also be used to butcher corpses."

#. ~ Description for kris
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This wavy bladed dagger comes from Southeast Asia.  The design of the blade "
"causes it to make broad, painful wounds."
msgstr "This wavy bladed dagger comes from Southeast Asia.  The design of the blade causes it to make broad, painful wounds."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "kukri"
msgid_plural "kukris"
msgstr[0] "kukri"
msgstr[1] "kukris"

#. ~ Description for kukri
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This versatile implement is a modern take on a traditional weapon that "
"originated in Nepal.  Featuring a heavy blade with an inwardly curved edge, "
"it is used as both a tool and as a weapon."
msgstr "This versatile implement is a modern take on a traditional weapon that originated in Nepal.  Featuring a heavy blade with an inwardly curved edge, it is used as both a tool and as a weapon."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "L-stick (off)"
msgid_plural "l-sticks (off)"
msgstr[0] "L-stick (off)"
msgstr[1] "l-sticks (off)"

#. ~ Use action msg for L-stick (off).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The L-stick(tm) lights up."
msgstr "The L-stick(tm) lights up."

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for L-stick (off).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The L-stick(tm)'s batteries are empty."
msgstr "The L-stick(tm)'s batteries are empty."

#. ~ Description for L-stick (off)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Produced by the Light corporation, this stylish staff not only functions as "
"a light source, but doubles as a light-weight weapon, due to the superalloy "
"materials it is made of.  Due to proprietary efficiency improvements over "
"standard light sources, the l-stick or light stick as it is commonly called,"
" batteries last longer than other light sources."
msgstr "Produced by the Light corporation, this stylish staff not only functions as a light source, but doubles as a light-weight weapon, due to the superalloy materials it is made of.  Due to proprietary efficiency improvements over standard light sources, the l-stick or light stick as it is commonly called, batteries last longer than other light sources."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "L-stick (on)"
msgid_plural "L-sticks (on)"
msgstr[0] "L-stick (on)"
msgstr[1] "L-sticks (on)"

#. ~ Use action msg for L-stick (on).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The l-stick(tm)'s light fades away."
msgstr "The l-stick(tm)'s light fades away."

#. ~ Description for L-stick (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Produced by the Light corporation, this stylish staff not only functions as "
"a light source, but doubles as a light-weight weapon, due to the superalloy "
"materials it is made of.  Due to proprietary efficiency improvements over "
"standard light sources, the l-stick or light stick as it is commonly called,"
" batteries last longer than other light sources.  The staff is glowing "
"brightly, which is slowly draining the batteries."
msgstr "Produced by the Light corporation, this stylish staff not only functions as a light source, but doubles as a light-weight weapon, due to the superalloy materials it is made of.  Due to proprietary efficiency improvements over standard light sources, the l-stick or light stick as it is commonly called, batteries last longer than other light sources.  The staff is glowing brightly, which is slowly draining the batteries."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
msgid "land mine"
msgid_plural "land mines"
msgstr[0] "land mine"
msgstr[1] "land mines"

#. ~ Use action done_message for land mine.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You set the land mine."
msgstr "You set the land mine."

#. ~ Use action bury_question for land mine.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Bury the land mine?"
msgstr "Bury the land mine?"

#. ~ Use action done_message for land mine.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You bury the land mine."
msgstr "You bury the land mine."

#. ~ Description for land mine
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an military anti-personnel mine that is triggered when stepped upon."
msgstr "This is an military anti-personnel mine that is triggered when stepped upon."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "gunsmith repair kit"
msgid_plural "gunsmith repair kits"
msgstr[0] "gunsmith repair kit"
msgstr[1] "gunsmith repair kits"

#. ~ Description for gunsmith repair kit
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a complete toolkit made to repair damaged firearms.  Powered by "
"standard batteries, it is a vital tool for long-term firearms maintenance.  "
"It requires 25 charges of battery power per use."
msgstr "This is a complete toolkit made to repair damaged firearms.  Powered by standard batteries, it is a vital tool for long-term firearms maintenance.  It requires 25 charges of battery power per use."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "large tent"
msgid_plural "large tents"
msgstr[0] "large tent"
msgstr[1] "large tents"

#. ~ Description for large tent
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a family sized tent.  It provides a large amount of space, but is "
"very bulky."
msgstr "This is a family sized tent.  It provides a large amount of space, but is very bulky."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "leather funnel"
msgid_plural "leather funnels"
msgstr[0] "leather funnel"
msgstr[1] "leather funnels"

#. ~ Use action done_message for leather funnel.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You place the leather funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "You place the leather funnel, waiting to collect rain."

#. ~ Description for leather funnel
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small, leather funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside "
"and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr "This is a small, leather funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "light snare kit"
msgid_plural "light snare kits"
msgstr[0] "light snare kit"
msgstr[1] "light snare kits"

#. ~ Description for light snare kit
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a kit for a simple trap consisting of a string noose and a snare "
"trigger.  It requires a young tree nearby.  It is effective at trapping and "
"killing some small animals."
msgstr "This is a kit for a simple trap consisting of a string noose and a snare trigger.  It requires a young tree nearby.  It is effective at trapping and killing some small animals."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "lighter"
msgid_plural "lighters"
msgstr[0] "lighter"
msgstr[1] "lighters"

#. ~ Description for lighter
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a disposable plastic lighter.  A lighter must be carried to use "
"various drugs, like cigarettes, or to light things like Molotov cocktails.  "
"You can also use a lighter to light nearby items on fire."
msgstr "This is a disposable plastic lighter.  A lighter must be carried to use various drugs, like cigarettes, or to light things like Molotov cocktails.  You can also use a lighter to light nearby items on fire."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "lightstrip"
msgid_plural "lightstrips"
msgstr[0] "lightstrip"
msgstr[1] "lightstrips"

#. ~ Description for lightstrip
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a light-emitting circuit wired directly to some batteries.  It "
"provides some weak light and can't be turned off.  When the batteries die, "
"you'll need to scrap it to recover the components that are reusable."
msgstr "This is a light-emitting circuit wired directly to some batteries.  It provides some weak light and can't be turned off.  When the batteries die, you'll need to scrap it to recover the components that are reusable."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "lightstrip (unpowered)"
msgid_plural "lightstrips (unpowered)"
msgstr[0] "lightstrip (unpowered)"
msgstr[1] "lightstrips (unpowered)"

#. ~ Description for lightstrip (unpowered)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a unpowered lightstrip.  You could connect it to batteries to get a "
"light-emitting circuit."
msgstr "This is a unpowered lightstrip.  You could connect it to batteries to get a light-emitting circuit."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "lightstrip (inactive)"
msgid_plural "lightstrips (inactive)"
msgstr[0] "lightstrip (inactive)"
msgstr[1] "lightstrips (inactive)"

#. ~ Use action msg for lightstrip (inactive).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You irreversibly activate the lightstrip."
msgstr "You irreversibly activate the lightstrip."

#. ~ Description for lightstrip (inactive)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a light-emitting circuit wired directly to some batteries.  It will "
"provide some weak light once activated and can't be turned off.  When the "
"batteries die, you'll need to scrap it to recover the components that are "
"reusable."
msgstr "This is a light-emitting circuit wired directly to some batteries.  It will provide some weak light once activated and can't be turned off.  When the batteries die, you'll need to scrap it to recover the components that are reusable."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "lobotomizer"
msgid_plural "lobotomizers"
msgstr[0] "lobotomizer"
msgstr[1] "lobotomizers"

#. ~ Description for lobotomizer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hand-forged collapsible tool that has two axe heads and sharp "
"shovel-like tip on one end.  It can be used as a shovel, or you could chop "
"some zombies with it instead."
msgstr "This is a hand-forged collapsible tool that has two axe heads and sharp shovel-like tip on one end.  It can be used as a shovel, or you could chop some zombies with it instead."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "machete"
msgid_plural "machetes"
msgstr[0] "machete"
msgstr[1] "machetes"

#. ~ Description for machete
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This huge steel knife makes an excellent tool for cutting down large "
"vegetation or other 'obstacles.'"
msgstr "This huge steel knife makes an excellent tool for cutting down large vegetation or other 'obstacles.'"

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "magnifying glass"
msgid_plural "magnifying glasses"
msgstr[0] "magnifying glass"
msgstr[1] "magnifying glasses"

#. ~ Description for magnifying glass
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a magnifying glass.  May be useful for starting fires during sunny "
"skies."
msgstr "This is a magnifying glass.  May be useful for starting fires during sunny skies."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift crowbar"
msgid_plural "makeshift crowbars"
msgstr[0] "makeshift crowbar"
msgstr[1] "makeshift crowbars"

#. ~ Description for makeshift crowbar
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a pipe whose ends have been bent and hammered flat to resemble a "
"crowbar.  Use it to open locked doors without destroying them, or to lift "
"manhole covers.  You could also wield it to fight with, in a pinch."
msgstr "This is a pipe whose ends have been bent and hammered flat to resemble a crowbar.  Use it to open locked doors without destroying them, or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to fight with, in a pinch."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift funnel"
msgid_plural "makeshift funnels"
msgstr[0] "makeshift funnel"
msgstr[1] "makeshift funnels"

#. ~ Use action done_message for makeshift funnel.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You place the makeshift funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "You place the makeshift funnel, waiting to collect rain."

#. ~ Description for makeshift funnel
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small, makeshift funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside"
" and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr "This is a small, makeshift funnel used to collect rainwater.  Use it outside and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift hammer"
msgid_plural "makeshift hammers"
msgstr[0] "makeshift hammer"
msgstr[1] "makeshift hammers"

#. ~ Description for makeshift hammer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a crude hammer make from a piece of metal affixed to a stick.  It "
"functions adequately as a hammer, but really can't compare to a proper one."
msgstr "This is a crude hammer make from a piece of metal affixed to a stick.  It functions adequately as a hammer, but really can't compare to a proper one."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift knife"
msgid_plural "makeshift knives"
msgstr[0] "makeshift knife"
msgstr[1] "makeshift knives"

#. ~ Description for makeshift knife
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A knife consisting of a long, somewhat sharpened, spike and a tightly "
"wrapped rag as a handle.  It makes a good melee weapon."
msgstr "A knife consisting of a long, somewhat sharpened, spike and a tightly wrapped rag as a handle.  It makes a good melee weapon."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift machete"
msgid_plural "makeshift machetes"
msgstr[0] "makeshift machete"
msgstr[1] "makeshift machetes"

#. ~ Description for makeshift machete
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a large blade that has had a portion of the handle wrapped in duct "
"tape, making it easier to wield as a rough machete."
msgstr "This is a large blade that has had a portion of the handle wrapped in duct tape, making it easier to wield as a rough machete."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift vacuum sealer"
msgid_plural "makeshift vacuum sealers"
msgstr[0] "makeshift vacuum sealer"
msgstr[1] "makeshift vacuum sealers"

#. ~ Description for makeshift vacuum sealer
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a homemade heat sealer unit with an air pump.  It's used for vacuum "
"packing food to preserve it."
msgstr "This is a homemade heat sealer unit with an air pump.  It's used for vacuum packing food to preserve it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "match head bomb"
msgid_plural "match head bombs"
msgstr[0] "match head bomb"
msgstr[1] "match head bombs"

#. ~ Use action msg for match head bomb.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You light the match head bomb."
msgstr "You light the match head bomb."

#. ~ Description for match head bomb
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a homemade bomb consisting of a bottle filled with match heads and "
"equipped with a fuse.  Use this item to light the fuse; you will, of course,"
" need a lighter in your inventory to do this."
msgstr "This is a homemade bomb consisting of a bottle filled with match heads and equipped with a fuse.  Use this item to light the fuse; you will, of course, need a lighter in your inventory to do this."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "match head bomb (lit)"
msgid_plural "match head bombs (lit)"
msgstr[0] "match head bomb (lit)"
msgstr[1] "match head bombs (lit)"

#. ~ Description for match head bomb (lit)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a bottle filled with match heads and equipped with a fuse.  This one"
" has been lit, and its fuse is rapidly burning down.  You may not want to "
"hold onto it much longer."
msgstr "This is a bottle filled with match heads and equipped with a fuse.  This one has been lit, and its fuse is rapidly burning down.  You may not want to hold onto it much longer."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "matchbook"
msgid_plural "matchbooks"
msgstr[0] "matchbook"
msgstr[1] "matchbooks"

#. ~ Description for matchbook
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small book of matches with a coarse strike surface on the outside "
"flap.  Matches must be carried to use various drugs like cigarettes, or to "
"light things like Molotov cocktails.  You can also use matches to light "
"nearby items on fire."
msgstr "This is a small book of matches with a coarse strike surface on the outside flap.  Matches must be carried to use various drugs like cigarettes, or to light things like Molotov cocktails.  You can also use matches to light nearby items on fire."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "mess kit"
msgid_plural "mess kits"
msgstr[0] "mess kit"
msgstr[1] "mess kits"

#. ~ Description for mess kit
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A self-contained camping mess kit, containing everything you might need for "
"wilderness cooking.  This model relies on a battery-operated hotplate, "
"rather than the more commonplace chemical-fueled Esbit stove."
msgstr "A self-contained camping mess kit, containing everything you might need for wilderness cooking.  This model relies on a battery-operated hotplate, rather than the more commonplace chemical-fueled Esbit stove."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py lang/json/trap_from_json.py
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "metal funnel"
msgid_plural "metal funnels"
msgstr[0] "metal funnel"
msgstr[1] "metal funnels"

#. ~ Use action done_message for metal funnel.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You place the metal funnel, waiting to collect rain."
msgstr "You place the metal funnel, waiting to collect rain."

#. ~ Description for metal funnel
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a large metal funnel used to collect rainwater.  Less portable than "
"plastic funnels, but collects more water.  Use it outside and place a "
"container beneath it to collect water when it rains."
msgstr "This is a large metal funnel used to collect rainwater.  Less portable than plastic funnels, but collects more water.  Use it outside and place a container beneath it to collect water when it rains."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "metallic smoother"
msgid_plural "metallic smoothers"
msgstr[0] "metallic smoother"
msgstr[1] "metallic smoothers"

#. ~ Description for metallic smoother
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This metallic tool is most often used to smooth concrete, or mortar, in "
"construction projects."
msgstr "This metallic tool is most often used to smooth concrete, or mortar, in construction projects."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "military mess kit"
msgid_plural "military mess kits"
msgstr[0] "military mess kit"
msgstr[1] "military mess kits"

#. ~ Description for military mess kit
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Military mess kit designed for long-range reconnaissance patrols deployed "
"behind enemy lines.  All parts are made from thin sheet of aluminum / "
"superalloy composite and are insulated with ceramic coating.  Relies on a "
"battery-operated hotplate, rather than the smoke-producing chemical-fueled "
"Esbit stove.  Compact, durable and lightweight."
msgstr "Military mess kit designed for long-range reconnaissance patrols deployed behind enemy lines.  All parts are made from thin sheet of aluminum / superalloy composite and are insulated with ceramic coating.  Relies on a battery-operated hotplate, rather than the smoke-producing chemical-fueled Esbit stove.  Compact, durable and lightweight."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "mininuke"
msgid_plural "mininukes"
msgstr[0] "mininuke"
msgstr[1] "mininukes"

#. ~ Description for mininuke
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an extremely powerful weapon--essentially a hand-held nuclear bomb."
"  Use it to activate the timer.  You guess that the explosion would be large"
" enough to take out a small house."
msgstr "This is an extremely powerful weapon--essentially a hand-held nuclear bomb.  Use it to activate the timer.  You guess that the explosion would be large enough to take out a small house."

#. ~ Description for mininuke
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This miniature nuclear bomb has a light blinking on the side, showing that "
"it will soon explode.  You should probably get far, far away from it."
msgstr "This miniature nuclear bomb has a light blinking on the side, showing that it will soon explode.  You should probably get far, far away from it."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "basic repair kit"
msgid_plural "basic repair kits"
msgstr[0] "basic repair kit"
msgstr[1] "basic repair kits"

#. ~ Description for basic repair kit
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a portable toolkit.  When supplied with duct tape, it serves as a "
"vital tool for fixing items made of wood, paper, bone, or chitin.  It "
"requires 50 units of duct tape per use."
msgstr "This is a portable toolkit.  When supplied with duct tape, it serves as a vital tool for fixing items made of wood, paper, bone, or chitin.  It requires 50 units of duct tape per use."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "plastic mold"
msgid_plural "plastic molds"
msgstr[0] "plastic mold"
msgstr[1] "plastic molds"

#. ~ Description for plastic mold
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a plastic mold.  It could be shaped and used to craft items made of "
"plastic."
msgstr "This is a plastic mold.  It could be shaped and used to craft items made of plastic."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Molotov cocktail"
msgid_plural "Molotov cocktails"
msgstr[0] "Molotov cocktail"
msgstr[1] "Molotov cocktails"

#. ~ Use action msg for Molotov cocktail.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You light the Molotov cocktail."
msgstr "You light the Molotov cocktail."

#. ~ Description for Molotov cocktail
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A bottle of flammable liquid with a rag inserted.  Use this item to light "
"the rag.  You will, of course, need a lighter or matches in your inventory "
"to do this.  After lighting it, throw it to cause fires."
msgstr "A bottle of flammable liquid with a rag inserted.  Use this item to light the rag.  You will, of course, need a lighter or matches in your inventory to do this.  After lighting it, throw it to cause fires."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Molotov cocktail (lit)"
msgid_plural "Molotov cocktails (lit)"
msgstr[0] "Molotov cocktail (lit)"
msgstr[1] "Molotov cocktails (lit)"

#. ~ Description for Molotov cocktail (lit)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A bottle of flammable liquid with a flaming rag inserted.  Throwing it will "
"cause the bottle to break, spreading fire.  The flame may go out shortly if "
"you do not throw it.  Dropping it while lit is not safe."
msgstr "A bottle of flammable liquid with a flaming rag inserted.  Throwing it will cause the bottle to break, spreading fire.  The flame may go out shortly if you do not throw it.  Dropping it while lit is not safe."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "mop"
msgid_plural "mops"
msgstr[0] "mop"
msgstr[1] "mops"

#. ~ Description for mop
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an unwieldy mop.  Good for cleaning up spills.  Use to mop up any "
"'mess' you may have made."
msgstr "This is an unwieldy mop.  Good for cleaning up spills.  Use to mop up any 'mess' you may have made."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "mp3 player (off)"
msgid_plural "mp3 players (off)"
msgstr[0] "mp3 player (off)"
msgstr[1] "mp3 players (off)"

#. ~ Description for mp3 player (off)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This battery-devouring device is loaded up with someone's music collection."
"  Fortunately, there's lots of songs you like, and listening to it will "
"raise your morale slightly.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr "This battery-devouring device is loaded up with someone's music collection.  Fortunately, there's lots of songs you like, and listening to it will raise your morale slightly.  Use it to turn it on."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "mp3 player (on)"
msgid_plural "mp3 players (on)"
msgstr[0] "mp3 player (on)"
msgstr[1] "mp3 players (on)"

#. ~ Description for mp3 player (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This mp3 player is turned on and playing some great tunes, raising your "
"morale steadily while on your person.  It runs through batteries quickly; "
"you can turn it off by using it.  It also obscures your hearing."
msgstr "This mp3 player is turned on and playing some great tunes, raising your morale steadily while on your person.  It runs through batteries quickly; you can turn it off by using it.  It also obscures your hearing."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "multi cooker"
msgid_plural "multi cookers"
msgstr[0] "multi cooker"
msgstr[1] "multi cookers"

#. ~ Description for multi cooker
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A professional-grade multi-cooker, with a battery slot for camping trips or "
"tailgating.  Its multitude of settings and features promise to handle any "
"sort of cooking, from parboiling potatoes to cooking curry to popping "
"popcorn.  There's no manual, but you're sure you can work it out."
msgstr "A professional-grade multi-cooker, with a battery slot for camping trips or tailgating.  Its multitude of settings and features promise to handle any sort of cooking, from parboiling potatoes to cooking curry to popping popcorn.  There's no manual, but you're sure you can work it out."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "multi-tool"
msgid_plural "multi-tools"
msgstr[0] "multi-tool"
msgstr[1] "multi-tools"

#. ~ Description for multi-tool
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A cleverly designed all-in-one tool which combines several smaller tools "
"into the handles of a pair of pliers."
msgstr "A cleverly designed all-in-one tool which combines several smaller tools into the handles of a pair of pliers."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "bone needle"
msgid_plural "bone needles"
msgstr[0] "bone needle"
msgstr[1] "bone needles"

#. ~ Description for bone needle
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is sharp needle made from a bone.  It would be useful for making rough "
"clothing and items.  Its low quality makes it rather unsuitable for anything"
" requiring speed or precision."
msgstr "This is sharp needle made from a bone.  It would be useful for making rough clothing and items.  Its low quality makes it rather unsuitable for anything requiring speed or precision."

