msgid_plural "scissor jacks"
msgstr[0] "scissor jack"
msgstr[1] "scissor jacks"

#. ~ Description for scissor jack
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "A compact scissor jack used for lifting vehicles."
msgstr "A compact scissor jack used for lifting vehicles."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "acetylene torch"
msgid_plural "acetylene torches"
msgstr[0] "acetylene torch"
msgstr[1] "acetylene torches"

#. ~ Description for acetylene torch
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A compact tool kit intended for welding and cutting metal, this portable "
"oxyacetylene torch includes a torch handle and cutting attachment in an "
"easy-to-carry tote.  It requires connecting to pressurized cylinders of an "
"appropriate welding gas before use.  In addition to its metalworking uses, "
"you can activate it in order to destroy metal barriers."
msgstr "A compact tool kit intended for welding and cutting metal, this portable oxyacetylene torch includes a torch handle and cutting attachment in an easy-to-carry tote.  It requires connecting to pressurized cylinders of an appropriate welding gas before use.  In addition to its metalworking uses, you can activate it in order to destroy metal barriers."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "offering chalice"
msgid_plural "offering chalices"
msgstr[0] "offering chalice"
msgstr[1] "offering chalices"

#. ~ Use action msg for offering chalice.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You raise the chalice to your lips..."
msgstr "You raise the chalice to your lips..."

#. ~ Description for offering chalice
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a strange chalice made of gold, engraved all over with some "
"unfamiliar text.  It is filled with a thick black liquid that you seem "
"unable to pour out.  You get the feeling that trying to drink it would be a "
"bad idea."
msgstr "This is a strange chalice made of gold, engraved all over with some unfamiliar text.  It is filled with a thick black liquid that you seem unable to pour out.  You get the feeling that trying to drink it would be a bad idea."

#. ~ Use action activation_message for offering chalice.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"As you drink from the chalice, you feel your breath being drawn from your "
"lungs!"
msgstr "As you drink from the chalice, you feel your breath being drawn from your lungs!"

#. ~ Description for offering chalice
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a strange chalice made of gold, engraved all over with some "
"unfamiliar text.  Maybe you shouldn't be trying to drink from this..."
msgstr "This is a strange chalice made of gold, engraved all over with some unfamiliar text.  Maybe you shouldn't be trying to drink from this..."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "drained offering chalice"
msgid_plural "drained offering chalices"
msgstr[0] "drained offering chalice"
msgstr[1] "drained offering chalices"

#. ~ Description for drained offering chalice
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a strange chalice made of gold, engraved all over with some "
"unfamiliar text.  It appears to be empty, but you get the feeling that "
"something remains within it.  If you knew the right ritual..."
msgstr "This is a strange chalice made of gold, engraved all over with some unfamiliar text.  It appears to be empty, but you get the feeling that something remains within it.  If you knew the right ritual..."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "silver athame"
msgid_plural "silver athames"
msgstr[0] "silver athame"
msgstr[1] "silver athames"

#. ~ Use action msg for silver athame.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The edge of the athame looks too dull to break the skin, yet some strange "
"urge leads you to test this..."
msgstr "The edge of the athame looks too dull to break the skin, yet some strange urge leads you to test this..."

#. ~ Description for silver athame
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An ornate silver dagger, seemingly made for ritual purposes.  It seems "
"sharper than silver has any right to be."
msgstr "An ornate silver dagger, seemingly made for ritual purposes.  It seems sharper than silver has any right to be."

#. ~ Use action activation_message for silver athame.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Upon drawing the blade across your palm, wounds open elsewhere on your body!"
msgstr "Upon drawing the blade across your palm, wounds open elsewhere on your body!"

#. ~ Description for silver athame
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An ornate silver dagger, seemingly made for ritual purposes.  This seems "
"like a stupid idea..."
msgstr "An ornate silver dagger, seemingly made for ritual purposes.  This seems like a stupid idea..."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "incorruptible sword"
msgid_plural "incorruptible swords"
msgstr[0] "incorruptible sword"
msgstr[1] "incorruptible swords"

#. ~ Use action success_message for incorruptible sword.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The blade gives off a brilliant glow as you invoke its power!"
msgstr "The blade gives off a brilliant glow as you invoke its power!"

#. ~ Use action lacks_fuel_message for incorruptible sword.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The sword needs energy to serve its purpose."
msgstr "The sword needs energy to serve its purpose."

#. ~ Description for incorruptible sword
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is some sort of broadsword, decorated with a golden cross motif on the "
"blade.  When powered by consecrated magical essence, it has the power to cut"
" through darkness itself."
msgstr "This is some sort of broadsword, decorated with a golden cross motif on the blade.  When powered by consecrated magical essence, it has the power to cut through darkness itself."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "incorruptible sword (on)"
msgid_plural "incorruptible swords (on)"
msgstr[0] "incorruptible sword (on)"
msgstr[1] "incorruptible swords (on)"

#. ~ Use action charges_extinguish_message for incorruptible sword (on).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The sword's radiance fades."
msgstr "The sword's radiance fades."

#. ~ Use action voluntary_extinguish_message for incorruptible sword (on).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The blade dims as you dispel its effect."
msgstr "The blade dims as you dispel its effect."

#. ~ Use action water_extinguish_message for incorruptible sword (on).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The sword shimmers in the water, before the glow fades."
msgstr "The sword shimmers in the water, before the glow fades."

#. ~ Use action noise_message for incorruptible sword (on).
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "The glow intensifies, the blade yearning to cleave darkness itself."
msgstr "The glow intensifies, the blade yearning to cleave darkness itself."

#. ~ Description for incorruptible sword (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is some sort of broadsword, decorated with a golden cross motif on the "
"blade.  The blade is giving off an intense white light, and searing heat."
msgstr "This is some sort of broadsword, decorated with a golden cross motif on the blade.  The blade is giving off an intense white light, and searing heat."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "hammer of the hunter"
msgid_plural "hammers of the hunter"
msgstr[0] "hammer of the hunter"
msgstr[1] "hammers of the hunter"

#. ~ Use action msg for hammer of the hunter.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "\"Ave martello!\" The hammer gives off a golden light."
msgstr "\"Ave martello!\" The hammer gives off a golden light."

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for hammer of the hunter.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Dull essence shall make the hammer shine."
msgstr "Dull essence shall make the hammer shine."

#. ~ Description for hammer of the hunter
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A warhammer inlaid with silver, engraved with religious invocations in an "
"archaic form of Latin.  Many magical items can be purified with this item.  "
"Using it will channel consecrated essence into a stunning flash, though "
"using it is a double-edged sword."
msgstr "A warhammer inlaid with silver, engraved with religious invocations in an archaic form of Latin.  Many magical items can be purified with this item.  Using it will channel consecrated essence into a stunning flash, though using it is a double-edged sword."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glowing hammer of the hunter"
msgid_plural "glowing hammers of the hunter"
msgstr[0] "glowing hammer of the hunter"
msgstr[1] "glowing hammers of the hunter"

#. ~ Use action no_deactivate_msg for glowing hammer of the hunter.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "\"Du nicht können halt Hammerzeit.\""
msgstr "\"Du nicht können halt Hammerzeit.\""

#. ~ Description for glowing hammer of the hunter
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A warhammer inlaid with silver, engraved with religious invocations in an "
"archaic form of Latin.  It is giving off a bright golden glow, soon to be "
"brighter still."
msgstr "A warhammer inlaid with silver, engraved with religious invocations in an archaic form of Latin.  It is giving off a bright golden glow, soon to be brighter still."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "spear of pestilence"
msgid_plural "spears of pestilence"
msgstr[0] "spear of pestilence"
msgstr[1] "spears of pestilence"

#. ~ Description for spear of pestilence
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stout steel spear with a wicked sting, decorated with elaborate patterns "
"carved from chitin.  Using it will attempt to summon giant insects."
msgstr "A stout steel spear with a wicked sting, decorated with elaborate patterns carved from chitin.  Using it will attempt to summon giant insects."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of trickery"
msgid_plural "glyphs of trickery"
msgstr[0] "glyph of trickery"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of trickery"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of trickery.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The kreck looks up at you expectantly, as if wondering what sort of "
"shenanigans you're plotting."
msgstr "The kreck looks up at you expectantly, as if wondering what sort of shenanigans you're plotting."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of trickery.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The kreck mimics your movements erratically, cavorting about to mock you!"
msgstr "The kreck mimics your movements erratically, cavorting about to mock you!"

#. ~ Description for glyph of trickery
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with depictions of grotesque creatures.  "
"Using it will call forth a kreck, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with depictions of grotesque creatures.  Using it will call forth a kreck, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of impassiveness"
msgid_plural "glyphs of impassiveness"
msgstr[0] "glyph of impassiveness"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of impassiveness"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of impassiveness.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The featureless visage of the blank body is indecipherable at first, but its"
" passive posture suggests friendliness."
msgstr "The featureless visage of the blank body is indecipherable at first, but its passive posture suggests friendliness."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of impassiveness.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The featureless visage of the blank body is indecipherable at first, but its"
" body language suggests hostility."
msgstr "The featureless visage of the blank body is indecipherable at first, but its body language suggests hostility."

#. ~ Description for glyph of impassiveness
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with the emotionless faces of unknown "
"beings.  Using it will call forth a blank body, and bind it to your will.  "
"Hopefully."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with the emotionless faces of unknown beings.  Using it will call forth a blank body, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of the beholder"
msgid_plural "glyphs of the beholder"
msgstr[0] "glyph of the beholder"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of the beholder"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of the beholder.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You meet the flaming's eye's gaze, and it is the first to blink.  It seems "
"to be friendly."
msgstr "You meet the flaming's eye's gaze, and it is the first to blink.  It seems to be friendly."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of the beholder.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The eye levels a wicked gaze upon you.  This is a staring contest you won't "
"win."
msgstr "The eye levels a wicked gaze upon you.  This is a staring contest you won't win."

#. ~ Description for glyph of the beholder
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with flame patterns.  Using it will call "
"forth a flaming eye, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with flame patterns.  Using it will call forth a flaming eye, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of Crawling Chaos"
msgid_plural "glyphs of Crawling Chaos"
msgstr[0] "glyph of Crawling Chaos"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of Crawling Chaos"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of Crawling Chaos.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The hunting horror is at your beck and call.  A gift from the Stalker among "
"the Stars?"
msgstr "The hunting horror is at your beck and call.  A gift from the Stalker among the Stars?"

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of Crawling Chaos.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You feel the gaze of Nyarlathotep upon you.  How foolish of you, to steal "
"the harrier of the Faceless God!"
msgstr "You feel the gaze of Nyarlathotep upon you.  How foolish of you, to steal the harrier of the Faceless God!"

#. ~ Description for glyph of Crawling Chaos
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, erratically engraved with indecipherable runes.  "
"Using it will call forth a hunting horror, and bind it to your will.  "
"Hopefully.  Using it during the day might be a bad idea."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, erratically engraved with indecipherable runes.  Using it will call forth a hunting horror, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully.  Using it during the day might be a bad idea."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of the eye"
msgid_plural "glyphs of the eye"
msgstr[0] "glyph of the eye"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of the eye"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of the eye.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The wyrm springs forth, seeming to regard you passively, or at least "
"ignoring your presence."
msgstr "The wyrm springs forth, seeming to regard you passively, or at least ignoring your presence."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of the eye.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The wyrm springs forth, reacting to unfamiliar sounds and scent with a "
"malevolent screech!"
msgstr "The wyrm springs forth, reacting to unfamiliar sounds and scent with a malevolent screech!"

#. ~ Description for glyph of the eye
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with a serpentine motif.  Using it will "
"call forth a dark wyrm, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully.  Using it "
"during the day might be a bad idea."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with a serpentine motif.  Using it will call forth a dark wyrm, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully.  Using it during the day might be a bad idea."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of Yuggoth"
msgid_plural "glyphs of Yuggoth"
msgstr[0] "glyph of Yuggoth"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of Yuggoth"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of Yuggoth.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You recite an incantation, and the mi-go's response is a quiet murmur in "
"some unknown language.  It seems to be friendly."
msgstr "You recite an incantation, and the mi-go's response is a quiet murmur in some unknown language.  It seems to be friendly."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of Yuggoth.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You begin to recite an incantation, only for the mi-go to parrot your words,"
" mocking your effort to control it!"
msgstr "You begin to recite an incantation, only for the mi-go to parrot your words, mocking your effort to control it!"

#. ~ Description for glyph of Yuggoth
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with depictions of strange chitinous "
"entities.  Using it will call forth a mi-go, and bind it to your will.  "
"Hopefully."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with depictions of strange chitinous entities.  Using it will call forth a mi-go, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of the golem"
msgid_plural "glyphs of the golem"
msgstr[0] "glyph of the golem"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of the golem"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of the golem.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You hear a strange burbling, the creature bound to your will."
msgstr "You hear a strange burbling, the creature bound to your will."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of the golem.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Eyes of flame meet your gaze, the creature resists your attempt to control "
"it!"
msgstr "Eyes of flame meet your gaze, the creature resists your attempt to control it!"

#. ~ Description for glyph of the golem
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with reversed writing in an unknown "
"language.  Using it will call forth a jabberwock, and bind it to your will."
"  Hopefully."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with reversed writing in an unknown language.  Using it will call forth a jabberwock, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of anthozoa"
msgid_plural "glyphs of anthozoa"
msgstr[0] "glyph of anthozoa"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of anthozoa"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of anthozoa.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The flying polyp twitches for a moment, before its movement steadies.  It "
"seems to be friendly."
msgstr "The flying polyp twitches for a moment, before its movement steadies.  It seems to be friendly."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of anthozoa.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The flying polyp twitches erratically, reacting to your presence with "
"apparent hostility!"
msgstr "The flying polyp twitches erratically, reacting to your presence with apparent hostility!"

#. ~ Description for glyph of anthozoa
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with an strange pattern resembling coral."
"  Using it will call forth a flying polyp, and bind it to your will.  "
"Hopefully."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with an strange pattern resembling coral.  Using it will call forth a flying polyp, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of the platyhelminthes"
msgid_plural "glyphs of the platyhelminthes"
msgstr[0] "glyph of the platyhelminthes"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of the platyhelminthes"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of the platyhelminthes.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"With the silver glyph as an offering, you bind the yugg to serve you.  You "
"feel like this is the opposite of how it normally works."
msgstr "With the silver glyph as an offering, you bind the yugg to serve you.  You feel like this is the opposite of how it normally works."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of the platyhelminthes.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An offering of wealth is not enough to placate a servant of Ubb.  The "
"creature turns hostile!"
msgstr "An offering of wealth is not enough to placate a servant of Ubb.  The creature turns hostile!"

#. ~ Description for glyph of the platyhelminthes
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with depictions of ancient, cthonian "
"wealth.  Using it will call forth a yugg, and bind it to your will.  "
"Hopefully."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with depictions of ancient, cthonian wealth.  Using it will call forth a yugg, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glyph of the Elder Things"
msgid_plural "glyphs of the Elder Things"
msgstr[0] "glyph of the Elder Things"
msgstr[1] "glyphs of the Elder Things"

#. ~ Use action friendly_msg for glyph of the Elder Things.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You hear a voice in your mind.  \"Tekili ...l-li?\"  Your mind exerts a "
"strange influence upon the shoggoth."
msgstr "You hear a voice in your mind.  \"Tekili ...l-li?\"  Your mind exerts a strange influence upon the shoggoth."

#. ~ Use action hostile_msg for glyph of the Elder Things.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You hear a voice in your mind.  \"Tekeli-li!\"  The shoggoth resists your "
"efforts to control it!"
msgstr "You hear a voice in your mind.  \"Tekeli-li!\"  The shoggoth resists your efforts to control it!"

#. ~ Description for glyph of the Elder Things
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strange silver emblem, engraved with many strange eye symbols.  Using it "
"will call forth a shoggoth, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."
msgstr "A strange silver emblem, engraved with many strange eye symbols.  Using it will call forth a shoggoth, and bind it to your will.  Hopefully."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "veinreaver"
msgid_plural "veinreavers"
msgstr[0] "veinreaver"
msgstr[1] "veinreavers"

#. ~ Use action msg for veinreaver.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You draw upon the axe's energy, and the axehead glows a bright red!"
msgstr "You draw upon the axe's energy, and the axehead glows a bright red!"

#. ~ Description for veinreaver
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hatchet with its axehead stained the dull color of dried blood, making it "
"appear rusted despite being in usable condition.  Using it will channel "
"blood essence into a nasty explosion."
msgstr "A hatchet with its axehead stained the dull color of dried blood, making it appear rusted despite being in usable condition.  Using it will channel blood essence into a nasty explosion."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "glowing veinreaver"
msgid_plural "glowing veinreavers"
msgstr[0] "glowing veinreaver"
msgstr[1] "glowing veinreavers"

#. ~ Use action sound_msg for glowing veinreaver.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Drip."
msgstr "Drip."

#. ~ Use action no_deactivate_msg for glowing veinreaver.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "You can't dispel the effect.  Might want to try throwing it instead."
msgstr "You can't dispel the effect.  Might want to try throwing it instead."

#. ~ Description for glowing veinreaver
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hatchet, axehead giving off a wicked red glow.  Throwing it might be a "
"smart idea."
msgstr "A hatchet, axehead giving off a wicked red glow.  Throwing it might be a smart idea."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "scroll of light"
msgid_plural "scrolls of light"
msgstr[0] "scroll of light"
msgstr[1] "scrolls of light"

#. ~ Use action msg for scroll of light.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "\"Reveal that which is unseen.\"  You unroll the scroll of light..."
msgstr "\"Reveal that which is unseen.\"  You unroll the scroll of light..."

#. ~ Description for scroll of light
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a scroll, with odd writing and illustrations of a solar motif on it."
"  Using it will brighten the sky."
msgstr "This is a scroll, with odd writing and illustrations of a solar motif on it.  Using it will brighten the sky."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "scroll of darkness"
msgid_plural "scrolls of mysticism"
msgstr[0] "scroll of darkness"
msgstr[1] "scrolls of mysticism"

#. ~ Use action msg for scroll of darkness.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "\"Do not fear the unknown.\"  You unroll the scroll of darkness..."
msgstr "\"Do not fear the unknown.\"  You unroll the scroll of darkness..."

#. ~ Description for scroll of darkness
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a scroll, with odd writing and depictions of the lunar cycles on it."
"  Using it will darken the sky temporarily."
msgstr "This is a scroll, with odd writing and depictions of the lunar cycles on it.  Using it will darken the sky temporarily."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "scroll of command"
msgid_plural "scrolls of command"
msgstr[0] "scroll of command"
msgstr[1] "scrolls of command"

#. ~ Use action msg for scroll of command.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"\"By order, we ascend beyond that of animals.\"  You unroll the scroll of "
"command..."
msgstr "\"By order, we ascend beyond that of animals.\"  You unroll the scroll of command..."

#. ~ Description for scroll of command
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a scroll, with odd writing and images of solders standing in "
"formation on it.  Using it will attempt to bind nearby creatures to your "
"will temporarily, at the expense of pain and momentary paralysis."
msgstr "This is a scroll, with odd writing and images of solders standing in formation on it.  Using it will attempt to bind nearby creatures to your will temporarily, at the expense of pain and momentary paralysis."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "scroll of overgrowth"
msgid_plural "scrolls of overgrowth"
msgstr[0] "scroll of overgrowth"
msgstr[1] "scrolls of overgrowth"

#. ~ Use action msg for scroll of overgrowth.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "\"Do not deny your instincts.\"  You unroll the scroll of overgrowth..."
msgstr "\"Do not deny your instincts.\"  You unroll the scroll of overgrowth..."

#. ~ Description for scroll of overgrowth
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a scroll, with odd writing and exotic natural scenery depicted on "
"it.  Using it will fill the area with life, causing plants to grow "
"unnaturally and healing you, potentially mutating you as well."
msgstr "This is a scroll, with odd writing and exotic natural scenery depicted on it.  Using it will fill the area with life, causing plants to grow unnaturally and healing you, potentially mutating you as well."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "scroll of sundering"
msgid_plural "scrolls of sundering"
msgstr[0] "scroll of sundering"
msgstr[1] "scrolls of sundering"

#. ~ Use action msg for scroll of sundering.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "\"There is an end to everything.\"  You unroll the scroll of sundering..."
msgstr "\"There is an end to everything.\"  You unroll the scroll of sundering..."

#. ~ Description for scroll of sundering
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a scroll, with odd writing and scenes of natural disasters on it.  "
"Using it will call forth a horrid noise, toppling nearby structures and "
"harming creatures around you.  It might attract unwanted attention as well."
msgstr "This is a scroll, with odd writing and scenes of natural disasters on it.  Using it will call forth a horrid noise, toppling nearby structures and harming creatures around you.  It might attract unwanted attention as well."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "scroll of discord"
msgid_plural "scrolls of discord"
msgstr[0] "scroll of discord"
msgstr[1] "scrolls of discord"

#. ~ Use action msg for scroll of discord.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "\"Cast aside the veil of reality.\"  You unroll the scroll of discord..."
msgstr "\"Cast aside the veil of reality.\"  You unroll the scroll of discord..."

#. ~ Description for scroll of discord
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a scroll, with odd writing and peculiar swirling symbols on it.  "
"Using it will warp the fabric of space, teleporting you at random.  The trip"
" is a bit nauseating, and you might be followed."
msgstr "This is a scroll, with odd writing and peculiar swirling symbols on it.  Using it will warp the fabric of space, teleporting you at random.  The trip is a bit nauseating, and you might be followed."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "cursed blade"
msgid_plural "cursed blades"
msgstr[0] "cursed blade"
msgstr[1] "cursed blades"

#. ~ Use action msg for cursed blade.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The runes on the blade glow for a moment, and you feel a strange bloodlust "
"overtake you."
msgstr "The runes on the blade glow for a moment, and you feel a strange bloodlust overtake you."

#. ~ Use action need_charges_msg for cursed blade.
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "Nine motes of blood shall awaken the blade."
msgstr "Nine motes of blood shall awaken the blade."

#. ~ Description for cursed blade
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A two-handed sword, blade is made of a dark metal, engraved with exotic "
"runes.  Activating it will grant the wielder a powerful life-draining "
"weapon, but you won't be able to let go of it until it runs out of energy."
msgstr "A two-handed sword, blade is made of a dark metal, engraved with exotic runes.  Activating it will grant the wielder a powerful life-draining weapon, but you won't be able to let go of it until it runs out of energy."

#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "cursed blade (on)"
msgid_plural "cursed blades (on)"
msgstr[0] "cursed blade (on)"
msgstr[1] "cursed blades (on)"

#. ~ Description for cursed blade (on)
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid ""
