#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Rough out there, isn't it?"
msgstr "Rough out there, isn't it?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Ma'am, you really shouldn't be traveling out there."
msgstr "Ma'am, you really shouldn't be traveling out there."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I don't have any jobs for you."
msgstr "I don't have any jobs for you."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I don't have any more jobs for you."
msgstr "I don't have any more jobs for you."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I just have one job for you.  Want to hear about it?"
msgstr "I just have one job for you.  Want to hear about it?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I have another job for you.  Want to hear about it?"
msgstr "I have another job for you.  Want to hear about it?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I have several jobs for you.  Which should I describe?"
msgstr "I have several jobs for you.  Which should I describe?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I have several more jobs for you.  Which should I describe?"
msgstr "I have several more jobs for you.  Which should I describe?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You're not working on anything for me right now."
msgstr "You're not working on anything for me right now."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "What about it?"
msgstr "What about it?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Which job?"
msgstr "Which job?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Sure, here you go!"
msgstr "Sure, here you go!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Welcome marshal..."
msgstr "Welcome marshal..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Welcome..."
msgstr "Welcome..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Before you say anything else, we're full.  Few days ago we had an outbreak "
"due to lett'n in too many new refugees.  We do desperately need supplies and"
" are willing to trade what we can for it.  Pay top dollar for jerky if you "
"have any."
msgstr "Before you say anything else, we're full.  Few days ago we had an outbreak due to lett'n in too many new refugees.  We do desperately need supplies and are willing to trade what we can for it.  Pay top dollar for jerky if you have any."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"To be honest, we started out with six buses full of office workers and "
"soccer moms... after the refugee outbreak a day or two ago the more "
"courageous ones in our party ended up dead.  The only thing we want now is "
"to run enough trade through here to keep us alive.  Don't care who your "
"goods come from or how you got them, just don't bring trouble."
msgstr "To be honest, we started out with six buses full of office workers and soccer moms... after the refugee outbreak a day or two ago the more courageous ones in our party ended up dead.  The only thing we want now is to run enough trade through here to keep us alive.  Don't care who your goods come from or how you got them, just don't bring trouble."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, but the only way we're going to make it is if we keep our gates "
"buttoned fast.  The guards in the basement have orders to shoot on sight, if"
" you so much as peep your head in the lower levels.  I don't know what made "
"the scavengers out there so ruthless but some of us have had to kill our own"
" bloody kids... don't even think about strong arming us."
msgstr "I'm sorry, but the only way we're going to make it is if we keep our gates buttoned fast.  The guards in the basement have orders to shoot on sight, if you so much as peep your head in the lower levels.  I don't know what made the scavengers out there so ruthless but some of us have had to kill our own bloody kids... don't even think about strong arming us."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Well the refugees were staying here on the first floor when one their "
"parties tried to sneak a dying guy in through the loading bay, we ended up "
"being awoken to shrieks and screams. Maybe two dozen people died that night."
"  The remaining refugees were banished the next day and went on to form a "
"couple of scavenging bands.  I'd say we got twenty decent men or women still"
" here but our real strength comes from all of our business partners that are"
" accustomed to doing whatever is needed to survive."
msgstr "Well the refugees were staying here on the first floor when one their parties tried to sneak a dying guy in through the loading bay, we ended up being awoken to shrieks and screams. Maybe two dozen people died that night.  The remaining refugees were banished the next day and went on to form a couple of scavenging bands.  I'd say we got twenty decent men or women still here but our real strength comes from all of our business partners that are accustomed to doing whatever is needed to survive."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Can't say we've heard much.  Most these shelters seemed to have been "
"designed to make people feel safer... not actually aid in their survival.  "
"Our radio equipment is utter garbage that someone convinced the government "
"to buy, with no intention of it ever being used.  From the passing "
"scavengers I've heard nothing but prime loot'n spots and rumors of hordes."
msgstr "Can't say we've heard much.  Most these shelters seemed to have been designed to make people feel safer... not actually aid in their survival.  Our radio equipment is utter garbage that someone convinced the government to buy, with no intention of it ever being used.  From the passing scavengers I've heard nothing but prime loot'n spots and rumors of hordes."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Had one guy pop in here a while back saying he had tried to drive into "
"Syracuse after the outbreak.  Didn't even make it downtown before he ran "
"into a wall of the living dead that could stop a tank.  He hightailed it out"
" but claims there were several thousand at least.  Guess when you get a "
"bunch of them together they end up making enough noise to attract everyone "
"in the neighborhood.  Luckily we haven't had a mob like that pass by here."
msgstr "Had one guy pop in here a while back saying he had tried to drive into Syracuse after the outbreak.  Didn't even make it downtown before he ran into a wall of the living dead that could stop a tank.  He hightailed it out but claims there were several thousand at least.  Guess when you get a bunch of them together they end up making enough noise to attract everyone in the neighborhood.  Luckily we haven't had a mob like that pass by here."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Well, there is a party of about a dozen 'scavengers' that found some sort of"
" government facility.  They bring us a literal truck load of jumpsuits, "
"m4's, and canned food every week or so.  Since some of those guys got family"
" here, we've been doing alright.  As to where it is, I don't have the "
"foggiest of ideas."
msgstr "Well, there is a party of about a dozen 'scavengers' that found some sort of government facility.  They bring us a literal truck load of jumpsuits, m4's, and canned food every week or so.  Since some of those guys got family here, we've been doing alright.  As to where it is, I don't have the foggiest of ideas."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Sorry, last thing we need is another mouth to feed.  Most of us lack any "
"real survival skills so keeping our group small enough to survive on the "
"food random scavengers bring to trade with us is important."
msgstr "Sorry, last thing we need is another mouth to feed.  Most of us lack any real survival skills so keeping our group small enough to survive on the food random scavengers bring to trade with us is important."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I'm sorry, not a risk we are willing to take right now."
msgstr "I'm sorry, not a risk we are willing to take right now."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"There isn't a chance in hell!  We had one guy come in here with bloody fur "
"all over his body... well I guess that isn't all that strange but I'm pretty"
" sure whatever toxic waste is still out there is bound to mutate more than "
"just his hair."
msgstr "There isn't a chance in hell!  We had one guy come in here with bloody fur all over his body... well I guess that isn't all that strange but I'm pretty sure whatever toxic waste is still out there is bound to mutate more than just his hair."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Keep to yourself and you won't find any problems."
msgstr "Keep to yourself and you won't find any problems."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I haven't been here for long but I do my best to watch who comes and goes.  "
"You can't always predict who will bring trouble."
msgstr "I haven't been here for long but I do my best to watch who comes and goes.  You can't always predict who will bring trouble."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Keep your head down and stay out of my way."
msgstr "Keep your head down and stay out of my way."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Like what?"
msgstr "Like what?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You're new here, who the hell put you up to this crap?"
msgstr "You're new here, who the hell put you up to this crap?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"If you don't get on with your business I'm going to have to ask you to leave"
" and not come back."
msgstr "If you don't get on with your business I'm going to have to ask you to leave and not come back."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "That's it, you're dead!"
msgstr "That's it, you're dead!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You must really have a death wish!"
msgstr "You must really have a death wish!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"We don't put-up with garbage like you, finish your business and get the hell"
" out."
msgstr "We don't put-up with garbage like you, finish your business and get the hell out."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I thought I smelled a pig.  I jest... please don't arrest me."
msgstr "I thought I smelled a pig.  I jest... please don't arrest me."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Huh, thought I smelled someone new. Can I help you?"
msgstr "Huh, thought I smelled someone new. Can I help you?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Oh, I didn't mean that in a bad way. Been out in the wilderness so long, I "
"find myself noticing things by scent before sight."
msgstr "Oh, I didn't mean that in a bad way. Been out in the wilderness so long, I find myself noticing things by scent before sight."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I trade food here in exchange for a place to crash and general supplies. "
"Well, more specifically I trade food that isn't stale chips and flat cola."
msgstr "I trade food here in exchange for a place to crash and general supplies. Well, more specifically I trade food that isn't stale chips and flat cola."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Not really, just trying to lead my life."
msgstr "Not really, just trying to lead my life."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Yep. Whatever game I spot, I bag and sell the meat and other parts here. Got"
" the occasional fish and basket full of wild fruit, but nothing comes close "
"to a freshly-cooked moose steak for supper!"
msgstr "Yep. Whatever game I spot, I bag and sell the meat and other parts here. Got the occasional fish and basket full of wild fruit, but nothing comes close to a freshly-cooked moose steak for supper!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Sure, just bagged a fresh batch of meat. You may want to grill it up before "
"it gets too, uh... 'tender'. "
msgstr "Sure, just bagged a fresh batch of meat. You may want to grill it up before it gets too, uh... 'tender'. "

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Feed a man a fish, he's full for a day. Feed a man a bullet, he's full for "
"the rest of his life."
msgstr "Feed a man a fish, he's full for a day. Feed a man a bullet, he's full for the rest of his life."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Spot your prey before something nastier spots you."
msgstr "Spot your prey before something nastier spots you."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I've heard that cougars sometimes leap. Maybe it's just a myth."
msgstr "I've heard that cougars sometimes leap. Maybe it's just a myth."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"The Jabberwock is real, don't listen to what anybody else says. If you see "
"it, RUN."
msgstr "The Jabberwock is real, don't listen to what anybody else says. If you see it, RUN."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Zombie animal meat isn't good for eating, but sometimes you might find "
"usable fur on 'em."
msgstr "Zombie animal meat isn't good for eating, but sometimes you might find usable fur on 'em."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"A steady diet of cooked meat and clean water will keep you alive forever, "
"but your taste buds and your colon may start to get angry at you. Eat a "
"piece of fruit every once in a while."
msgstr "A steady diet of cooked meat and clean water will keep you alive forever, but your taste buds and your colon may start to get angry at you. Eat a piece of fruit every once in a while."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Smoke crack to get more shit done."
msgstr "Smoke crack to get more shit done."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Watch your back out there."
msgstr "Watch your back out there."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Marshal..."
msgstr "Marshal..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Citizen..."
msgstr "Citizen..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm the region's federal liaison.  Most people here call us the 'Old Guard' "
"and I rather like the sound of it.  Despite how things currently appear, the"
" federal government was not entirely destroyed.  After the outbreak I was "
"chosen to coordinate civilian and militia efforts in support of military "
"operations."
msgstr "I'm the region's federal liaison.  Most people here call us the 'Old Guard' and I rather like the sound of it.  Despite how things currently appear, the federal government was not entirely destroyed.  After the outbreak I was chosen to coordinate civilian and militia efforts in support of military operations."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I ensure that the citizens here have what they need to survive and protect "
"themselves from raiders.  Keeping some form law is going to be the most "
"important  element in rebuilding the world.  We do what we can to keep the "
"'Free Merchants' here prospering and in return they have provided us with "
"spare men and supplies when they can."
msgstr "I ensure that the citizens here have what they need to survive and protect themselves from raiders.  Keeping some form law is going to be the most important  element in rebuilding the world.  We do what we can to keep the 'Free Merchants' here prospering and in return they have provided us with spare men and supplies when they can."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Well... I was like any other civilian till they conscripted me so I'll tell "
"it to you straight.  They're the  best hope we got right now.  They are "
"stretched impossibly thin but are willing to do what is needed to maintain "
"order.  They don't care much about looters since they understand most "
"everyone is dead, but if you have something they need... you WILL give it to"
" them.  Since most survivors have have nothing they want, they are welcomed "
"as champions."
msgstr "Well... I was like any other civilian till they conscripted me so I'll tell it to you straight.  They're the  best hope we got right now.  They are stretched impossibly thin but are willing to do what is needed to maintain order.  They don't care much about looters since they understand most everyone is dead, but if you have something they need... you WILL give it to them.  Since most survivors have have nothing they want, they are welcomed as champions."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"There isn't much pushed out by public relations that I'd actually believe.  "
"From what I gather, communication between the regional force commands is "
"almost non-existent.  What I do know is that the 'Old Guard' is currently "
"based out of the 2nd Fleet and patrols the Atlantic coast trying to provide "
"support to the remaining footholds."
msgstr "There isn't much pushed out by public relations that I'd actually believe.  From what I gather, communication between the regional force commands is almost non-existent.  What I do know is that the 'Old Guard' is currently based out of the 2nd Fleet and patrols the Atlantic coast trying to provide support to the remaining footholds."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I don't know much about how it formed but it is the armada of military and "
"commercial ships that's floating off the coast.  They have everything from "
"supertankers and carriers to fishing trawlers... even a few NATO ships.  "
"Most civilians are offered a cabin on one of the liners to retire to if they"
" serve as a federal employee for a few years."
msgstr "I don't know much about how it formed but it is the armada of military and commercial ships that's floating off the coast.  They have everything from supertankers and carriers to fishing trawlers... even a few NATO ships.  Most civilians are offered a cabin on one of the liners to retire to if they serve as a federal employee for a few years."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"They may just be propaganda but apparently one or two cities were successful"
" in 'walling themselves off.' Around here I was told that there were a few "
"places like this one but I couldn't tell you where."
msgstr "They may just be propaganda but apparently one or two cities were successful in 'walling themselves off.' Around here I was told that there were a few places like this one but I couldn't tell you where."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"You can't actually join unless you go through a recruiter.  We can usually "
"use help though, ask me from time to time if there is any work available.  "
"Completing missions as a contractor is a great way to make a name for "
"yourself among the most powerful men left in the world."
msgstr "You can't actually join unless you go through a recruiter.  We can usually use help though, ask me from time to time if there is any work available.  Completing missions as a contractor is a great way to make a name for yourself among the most powerful men left in the world."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Marshal, I'm afraid I can't talk now."
msgstr "Marshal, I'm afraid I can't talk now."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I'm not in charge here marshal."
msgstr "I'm not in charge here marshal."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I'm supposed to direct all questions to my leadership, marshal."
msgstr "I'm supposed to direct all questions to my leadership, marshal."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Hey, citizen... I'm not sure you belong here."
msgstr "Hey, citizen... I'm not sure you belong here."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You should mind your own business, nothing to see here."
msgstr "You should mind your own business, nothing to see here."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "If you need something you'll need to talk to someone else."
msgstr "If you need something you'll need to talk to someone else."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Dude, if you can hold your own you should look into enlisting."
msgstr "Dude, if you can hold your own you should look into enlisting."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Hey miss, don't you think it would be safer if you stuck with me?"
msgstr "Hey miss, don't you think it would be safer if you stuck with me?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Marshal, I hope you're here to assist us."
msgstr "Marshal, I hope you're here to assist us."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Sir, I don't know how the hell you got down here but if you have any sense "
"you'll get out while you can."
msgstr "Sir, I don't know how the hell you got down here but if you have any sense you'll get out while you can."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Ma'am, I don't know how the hell you got down here but if you have any sense"
" you'll get out while you can."
msgstr "Ma'am, I don't know how the hell you got down here but if you have any sense you'll get out while you can."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm leading what remains of my company on a mission to re-secure this "
"facility.  We entered the complex with two dozen men and immediately went "
"about securing this control room.  From here I dispatched my men to secure "
"vital systems located on this floor and the floors below this one.  If  we "
"are successful, this facility can be cleared and used as a permanent base of"
" operations in the region.  Most importantly it will allow us to redirect "
"refugee traffic away from overcrowded outposts and free up more of our "
"forces to conduct recovery operations."
msgstr "I'm leading what remains of my company on a mission to re-secure this facility.  We entered the complex with two dozen men and immediately went about securing this control room.  From here I dispatched my men to secure vital systems located on this floor and the floors below this one.  If  we are successful, this facility can be cleared and used as a permanent base of operations in the region.  Most importantly it will allow us to redirect refugee traffic away from overcrowded outposts and free up more of our forces to conduct recovery operations."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"This facility was constructed to provide a safe haven in the event of a "
"global conflict.  The vault can support several thousand people for a few "
"years if all systems are operational and sufficient notification is given.  "
"Unfortunately, the power system was damaged or sabotaged at some point and "
"released a single extremely lethal burst of radiation.  The catastrophic "
"event lasted for several minutes and resulted in the deaths of most people "
"located on the 2nd and lower floors.  Those working on this floor were able "
"to seal the access ways to the lower floors before succumbing to radiation "
"sickness.  The only other thing the logs tell us is that all water pressure "
"was diverted to the lower levels."
msgstr "This facility was constructed to provide a safe haven in the event of a global conflict.  The vault can support several thousand people for a few years if all systems are operational and sufficient notification is given.  Unfortunately, the power system was damaged or sabotaged at some point and released a single extremely lethal burst of radiation.  The catastrophic event lasted for several minutes and resulted in the deaths of most people located on the 2nd and lower floors.  Those working on this floor were able to seal the access ways to the lower floors before succumbing to radiation sickness.  The only other thing the logs tell us is that all water pressure was diverted to the lower levels."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Marshal, I'm rather surprised to see you here."
msgstr "Marshal, I'm rather surprised to see you here."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Sir you are not authorized to be here... you should leave."
msgstr "Sir you are not authorized to be here... you should leave."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Ma'am you are not authorized to be here... you should leave."
msgstr "Ma'am you are not authorized to be here... you should leave."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"We are securing the external communications array for this facility.  I'm "
"rather restricted in what I can release... go find my commander if you have "
"any questions."
msgstr "We are securing the external communications array for this facility.  I'm rather restricted in what I can release... go find my commander if you have any questions."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I was expecting the captain to send a runner.  Here is the list you are "
"looking for.  What we can identify from here are simply the frequencies that"
" have traffic on them.  Many of the transmissions are indecipherable without"
" repairing or replacing the equipment here.  When the facility was being "
"overrun, standard procedure was to destroy encryption hardware to protect "
"federal secrets and maintain the integrity of the comms network.  We are "
"hoping a few plain text messages can get picked up though."
msgstr "I was expecting the captain to send a runner.  Here is the list you are looking for.  What we can identify from here are simply the frequencies that have traffic on them.  Many of the transmissions are indecipherable without repairing or replacing the equipment here.  When the facility was being overrun, standard procedure was to destroy encryption hardware to protect federal secrets and maintain the integrity of the comms network.  We are hoping a few plain text messages can get picked up though."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I haven't done anything wrong..."
msgstr "I haven't done anything wrong..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm just a hired hand.  Someone pays me and I do what needs to be done."
msgstr "I'm just a hired hand.  Someone pays me and I do what needs to be done."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"If you have to fight your way out of an ambush, the only thing that is going"
" to save you is having a party that can return fire.  People who work alone "
"are easy pickings for monsters and bandits."
msgstr "If you have to fight your way out of an ambush, the only thing that is going to save you is having a party that can return fire.  People who work alone are easy pickings for monsters and bandits."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm currently waiting for a customer to return... I'll make you a deal "
"though,  $8,000 will cover my expenses if I get a small cut of the loot."
msgstr "I'm currently waiting for a customer to return... I'll make you a deal though,  $8,000 will cover my expenses if I get a small cut of the loot."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I guess you're the boss."
msgstr "I guess you're the boss."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Hope you're here to trade."
msgstr "Hope you're here to trade."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I oversee the food stocks for the center.  There was significant looting "
"during the panic when we first arrived so most of our food was carried away."
"  I manage what we have left and do everything I can to increase our "
"supplies.  Rot and mold are more significant in the damp basement so I "
"prioritize non-perishable food, such as cornmeal, jerky, and fruit wine."
msgstr "I oversee the food stocks for the center.  There was significant looting during the panic when we first arrived so most of our food was carried away.  I manage what we have left and do everything I can to increase our supplies.  Rot and mold are more significant in the damp basement so I prioritize non-perishable food, such as cornmeal, jerky, and fruit wine."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"All three are easy to locally produce in significant quantities and are non-"
"perishable.  We have a local farmer or two and a few hunter types that have "
"been making attempts to provide us with the nutritious supplies.  We do "
"always need more suppliers though.  Because this stuff is rather cheap in "
"bulk I can pay a premium for any you have on you.  Canned food and other "
"edibles are handled by the merchant in the front."
msgstr "All three are easy to locally produce in significant quantities and are non-perishable.  We have a local farmer or two and a few hunter types that have been making attempts to provide us with the nutritious supplies.  We do always need more suppliers though.  Because this stuff is rather cheap in bulk I can pay a premium for any you have on you.  Canned food and other edibles are handled by the merchant in the front."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm actually accepting a number of different foodstuffs: beer, sugar, flour,"
" smoked meat, smoked fish, cooking oil; and as mentioned before, jerky, "
"cornmeal, and fruit wine."
msgstr "I'm actually accepting a number of different foodstuffs: beer, sugar, flour, smoked meat, smoked fish, cooking oil; and as mentioned before, jerky, cornmeal, and fruit wine."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Pleasure doing business!"
msgstr "Pleasure doing business!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Can I help you marshal?"
msgstr "Can I help you marshal?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Morning sir, how can I help you?"
msgstr "Morning sir, how can I help you?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Morning ma'am, how can I help you?"
msgstr "Morning ma'am, how can I help you?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I was starting to wonder if they were really interested in the project or "
"were just trying to get rid of me."
msgstr "I was starting to wonder if they were really interested in the project or were just trying to get rid of me."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Ya, that representative from the Old Guard asked the two of us to come out "
"here and begin fortifying this place as a refugee camp.  I'm not sure how "
"fast he expects the two of us to get setup but we were assured additional "
"men were coming out here to assist us. "
msgstr "Ya, that representative from the Old Guard asked the two of us to come out here and begin fortifying this place as a refugee camp.  I'm not sure how fast he expects the two of us to get setup but we were assured additional men were coming out here to assist us. "

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Could easily be hundreds as far as I know.  They chose this ranch because of"
" its rather remote location, decent fence, and huge cleared field.  With as "
"much land as we have fenced off we could build a village if we had the "
"materials.  We would have tried to secure a small town or something but the "
"lack of good farmland and number of undead makes it more practical for us to"
" build from scratch.  The refugee center I came from is constantly facing "
"starvation and undead assaults."
msgstr "Could easily be hundreds as far as I know.  They chose this ranch because of its rather remote location, decent fence, and huge cleared field.  With as much land as we have fenced off we could build a village if we had the materials.  We would have tried to secure a small town or something but the lack of good farmland and number of undead makes it more practical for us to build from scratch.  The refugee center I came from is constantly facing starvation and undead assaults."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm the engineer in charge of turning this place into a working camp.  This "
"is going to be an uphill battle, we used most of our initial supplies "
"getting here and boarding up the windows.  I've got a huge list of tasks "
"that need to get done so if you could help us keep supplied I'd appreciate "
"it.  If you have material to drop off you can just back your vehicle into "
"here and dump it on the ground, we'll sort it."
msgstr "I'm the engineer in charge of turning this place into a working camp.  This is going to be an uphill battle, we used most of our initial supplies getting here and boarding up the windows.  I've got a huge list of tasks that need to get done so if you could help us keep supplied I'd appreciate it.  If you have material to drop off you can just back your vehicle into here and dump it on the ground, we'll sort it."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"My partner is in charge of fortifying this place, you should ask him about "
"what needs to be done."
msgstr "My partner is in charge of fortifying this place, you should ask him about what needs to be done."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Howdy."
msgstr "Howdy."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I was among one of the first groups of immigrants sent here to fortify the "
"outpost.  I might have exaggerated my construction skills to get the hell "
"out of the refugee center.  Unless you are a trader there isn't much work "
"there and food was really becoming scarce when I left."
msgstr "I was among one of the first groups of immigrants sent here to fortify the outpost.  I might have exaggerated my construction skills to get the hell out of the refugee center.  Unless you are a trader there isn't much work there and food was really becoming scarce when I left."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Come back later, I need to take care of a few things first."
msgstr "Come back later, I need to take care of a few things first."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm tasked out to the construction party but I might be able to show you a "
"few pointers that I've picked up."
msgstr "I'm tasked out to the construction party but I might be able to show you a few pointers that I've picked up."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You need something?"
msgstr "You need something?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm one of the migrants that got diverted to this outpost when I arrived at "
"the refugee center.  They said I was big enough to swing an ax so my "
"profession became lumberjack... didn't have any say in it.  If I want to eat"
" then I'll be cutting wood from now till kingdom come."
msgstr "I'm one of the migrants that got diverted to this outpost when I arrived at the refugee center.  They said I was big enough to swing an ax so my profession became lumberjack... didn't have any say in it.  If I want to eat then I'll be cutting wood from now till kingdom come."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"The rate is a bit steep but I still have my quotas that I need to fulfill.  "
"The logs will be dropped off in the garage at the entrance to the camp.  "
"I'll need a bit of time before I can deliver another load."
msgstr "The rate is a bit steep but I still have my quotas that I need to fulfill.  The logs will be dropped off in the garage at the entrance to the camp.  I'll need a bit of time before I can deliver another load."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Don't have much time to talk."
msgstr "Don't have much time to talk."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I turn the logs that laborers bring in into lumber to expand the outpost.  "
"Maintaining the saw is a chore but breaks the monotony."
msgstr "I turn the logs that laborers bring in into lumber to expand the outpost.  Maintaining the saw is a chore but breaks the monotony."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Bringing in logs is one of the few tasks we can give to the unskilled so I'd"
" be hurting them if I outsourced it.  Ask around though, I'm sure most "
"people could use a hand."
msgstr "Bringing in logs is one of the few tasks we can give to the unskilled so I'd be hurting them if I outsourced it.  Ask around though, I'm sure most people could use a hand."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I was sent here to assist in setting-up the farm.  Most of us have no real "
"skills that transfer from before the cataclysm so things are a bit of trial "
"and error."
msgstr "I was sent here to assist in setting-up the farm.  Most of us have no real skills that transfer from before the cataclysm so things are a bit of trial and error."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, I don't have anything to trade.  The work program here splits "
"what we produce between the refugee center, the farm, and ourselves.  If you"
" are a skilled laborer then you can trade your time for a bit of extra "
"income on the side.  Not much I can do to assist you as a farmer though."
msgstr "I'm sorry, I don't have anything to trade.  The work program here splits what we produce between the refugee center, the farm, and ourselves.  If you are a skilled laborer then you can trade your time for a bit of extra income on the side.  Not much I can do to assist you as a farmer though."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You mind?"
msgstr "You mind?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm just a lucky guy that went from being chased by the undead to the noble "
"life of a dirt farmer.  We get room and board but won't see a share of our "
"labor unless the crop is a success."
msgstr "I'm just a lucky guy that went from being chased by the undead to the noble life of a dirt farmer.  We get room and board but won't see a share of our labor unless the crop is a success."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I've got no time for you.  If you want to make a trade or need a job look "
"for the foreman or crop overseer."
msgstr "I've got no time for you.  If you want to make a trade or need a job look for the foreman or crop overseer."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I hope you are here to do business."
msgstr "I hope you are here to do business."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"My job is to manage our outpost's agricultural production.  I'm constantly "
"searching for trade partners and investors to increase our capacity.  If you"
" are interested I typically have tasks that I need assistance with."
msgstr "My job is to manage our outpost's agricultural production.  I'm constantly searching for trade partners and investors to increase our capacity.  If you are interested I typically have tasks that I need assistance with."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Please leave me alone..."
msgstr "Please leave me alone..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I was just a laborer till they could find me something a bit more permanent "
"but being constantly sick has prevented me from doing much of anything."
msgstr "I was just a laborer till they could find me something a bit more permanent but being constantly sick has prevented me from doing much of anything."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I don't know what you could do.  I've tried everything.  Just give me "
"time..."
msgstr "I don't know what you could do.  I've tried everything.  Just give me time..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I keep getting sick!  At first I thought it was something I ate but now it "
"seems like I can't keep anything down..."
msgstr "I keep getting sick!  At first I thought it was something I ate but now it seems like I can't keep anything down..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "How can I help you?"
msgstr "How can I help you?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I was a practicing nurse so I've taken over the medical responsibilities of "
"the outpost till we can locate a physician."
msgstr "I was a practicing nurse so I've taken over the medical responsibilities of the outpost till we can locate a physician."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I'm willing to pay a premium for medical supplies that you might be able to "
"scavenge up.  I also have a few miscellaneous jobs from time to time."
msgstr "I'm willing to pay a premium for medical supplies that you might be able to scavenge up.  I also have a few miscellaneous jobs from time to time."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I can take a look at you or your companions if you are injured."
msgstr "I can take a look at you or your companions if you are injured."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "That's the best I can do on short notice..."
msgstr "That's the best I can do on short notice..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I'm sorry, I don't have time to see you at the moment."
msgstr "I'm sorry, I don't have time to see you at the moment."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I imagine we might be able to work something out..."
msgstr "I imagine we might be able to work something out..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Don't mind me."
msgstr "Don't mind me."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I chop up useless vehicles for spare parts and raw materials.  If we can't "
"use a vehicle immediately we haul it into the ring we are building to "
"surround the outpost... it provides a measure of defense in the event that "
"we get attacked."
msgstr "I chop up useless vehicles for spare parts and raw materials.  If we can't use a vehicle immediately we haul it into the ring we are building to surround the outpost... it provides a measure of defense in the event that we get attacked."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I don't personally, the teams we send out to recover the vehicles usually "
"need a hand but can be hard to catch since they spend most of their time "
"outside the outpost."
msgstr "I don't personally, the teams we send out to recover the vehicles usually need a hand but can be hard to catch since they spend most of their time outside the outpost."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Welcome to the junk shop..."
msgstr "Welcome to the junk shop..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I organize scavenging runs to bring in supplies that we can't produce "
"ourselves.  I try and provide incentives to get migrants to join one of the "
"teams... its dangerous work but keeps our outpost alive.  Selling anything "
"we can't use helps keep us afloat with the traders.  If you wanted to drop "
"off a companion or two to assist in one of the runs, I'd appreciate it."
msgstr "I organize scavenging runs to bring in supplies that we can't produce ourselves.  I try and provide incentives to get migrants to join one of the teams... its dangerous work but keeps our outpost alive.  Selling anything we can't use helps keep us afloat with the traders.  If you wanted to drop off a companion or two to assist in one of the runs, I'd appreciate it."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"Are you interested in the scavenging runs or one of the other tasks that I "
"might have for you?"
msgstr "Are you interested in the scavenging runs or one of the other tasks that I might have for you?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Want a drink?"
msgstr "Want a drink?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"If it isn't obvious, I oversee the bar here.  The scavengers bring in old "
"world alcohol that we sell for special occasions.  For most that come "
"through here though, the drinks we brew ourselves are the only thing they "
"can afford."
msgstr "If it isn't obvious, I oversee the bar here.  The scavengers bring in old world alcohol that we sell for special occasions.  For most that come through here though, the drinks we brew ourselves are the only thing they can afford."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"We have a policy of keeping information to ourselves.  Ask the patrons if "
"you want to hear rumors or news."
msgstr "We have a policy of keeping information to ourselves.  Ask the patrons if you want to hear rumors or news."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Our selection is a bit limited at the moment."
msgstr "Our selection is a bit limited at the moment."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Can I interest you in a trim?"
msgstr "Can I interest you in a trim?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"What?  I'm a barber... I cut hair.  There's demand for cheap cuts and a "
"shave out here."
msgstr "What?  I'm a barber... I cut hair.  There's demand for cheap cuts and a shave out here."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I can't imagine what I'd need your assistance with."
msgstr "I can't imagine what I'd need your assistance with."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Stand still while I get my clippers..."
msgstr "Stand still while I get my clippers..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Well, I guess it's just us."
msgstr "Well, I guess it's just us."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "At least we've got shelter."
msgstr "At least we've got shelter."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I don't know, look for supplies and other survivors I guess."
msgstr "I don't know, look for supplies and other survivors I guess."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Maybe we should start boarding up this place."
msgstr "Maybe we should start boarding up this place."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"I suppose getting a car up and running should really be useful if we have to"
" disappear quickly from here."
msgstr "I suppose getting a car up and running should really be useful if we have to disappear quickly from here."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"We could look for one of those farms out here. They can provide plenty of "
"food and aren't close to the cities."
msgstr "We could look for one of those farms out here. They can provide plenty of food and aren't close to the cities."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid ""
"We should probably stay away from those cities, even if there's plenty of "
"useful stuff there."
msgstr "We should probably stay away from those cities, even if there's plenty of useful stuff there."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You just asked me for stuff; ask later."
msgstr "You just asked me for stuff; ask later."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Why should I share my equipment with you?"
msgstr "Why should I share my equipment with you?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Okay, here you go."
msgstr "Okay, here you go."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "<no>, and if you ask again, <ill_kill_you>!"
msgstr "<no>, and if you ask again, <ill_kill_you>!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "<no><punc> <fuck_you>!"
msgstr "<no><punc> <fuck_you>!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Shall we resume?"
msgstr "Shall we resume?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Sorry, but it doesn't seem I have anything to teach you."
msgstr "Sorry, but it doesn't seem I have anything to teach you."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Here's what I can teach you..."
msgstr "Here's what I can teach you..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Alright, let's begin."
msgstr "Alright, let's begin."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Not until I get some antibiotics..."
msgstr "Not until I get some antibiotics..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You asked me recently; ask again later."
msgstr "You asked me recently; ask again later."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Why should I travel with you?"
msgstr "Why should I travel with you?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You got it, I'm with you!"
msgstr "You got it, I'm with you!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Yeah... I don't think so."
msgstr "Yeah... I don't think so."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "What is it?"
msgstr "What is it?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "You're really leaving?"
msgstr "You're really leaving?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Alright.  You can lead now."
msgstr "Alright.  You can lead now."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "No.  I'm the leader here."
msgstr "No.  I'm the leader here."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid "%d.%d miles."
msgstr "%d.%d miles."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid "%d foot."
msgid_plural "%d feet."
msgstr[0] "%d foot."
msgstr[1] "%d feet."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I'm on watch."
msgstr "I'm on watch."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Not a bloody chance, I'm going to get left behind!"
msgstr "Not a bloody chance, I'm going to get left behind!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I'd prefer to keep that to myself."
msgstr "I'd prefer to keep that to myself."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I really don't feel comfortable doing so..."
msgstr "I really don't feel comfortable doing so..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "*is not engaging enemies."
msgstr "*is not engaging enemies."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "*is engaging nearby enemies."
msgstr "*is engaging nearby enemies."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "*is engaging weak enemies."
msgstr "*is engaging weak enemies."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "*is engaging enemies you attack."
msgstr "*is engaging enemies you attack."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "*is engaging enemies close enough to attack without moving."
msgstr "*is engaging enemies close enough to attack without moving."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "*is engaging all enemies."
msgstr "*is engaging all enemies."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgctxt "npc"
msgid "He"
msgstr "He"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgctxt "npc"
msgid "She"
msgstr "She"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid " %s will use silenced firearms."
msgstr " %s will use silenced firearms."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid " %s will use firearms."
msgstr " %s will use firearms."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid " %s will not use firearms."
msgstr " %s will not use firearms."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid " %s will use grenades."
msgstr " %s will use grenades."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid " %s will not use grenades."
msgstr " %s will not use grenades."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "What should I do?"
msgstr "What should I do?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "How should I aim?"
msgstr "How should I aim?"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Okay, no sudden movements..."
msgstr "Okay, no sudden movements..."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Keep your distance!"
msgstr "Keep your distance!"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Hey there, <name_g>."
msgstr "Hey there, <name_g>."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "This is my territory, <name_b>."
msgstr "This is my territory, <name_b>."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I'm holing up here for safety."
msgstr "I'm holing up here for safety."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I run the shop here."
msgstr "I run the shop here."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "I'm guarding this location."
msgstr "I'm guarding this location."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgctxt "npc"
msgid "her"
msgstr "her"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgctxt "npc"
msgid "his"
msgstr "his"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid "*drops %s weapon."
msgstr "*drops %s weapon."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "Now get out of here, before I kill you."
msgstr "Now get out of here, before I kill you."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "&You yell, but can't hear yourself."
msgstr "&You yell, but can't hear yourself."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
msgid "&You yell."
msgstr "&You yell."

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid "Str %d - %d"
msgstr "Str %d - %d"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
#, c-format
msgid "Dex %d - %d"
msgstr "Dex %d - %d"

#: src/npctalk.cpp
